:title("Swift (subset) to LLVM IR compiler") ;
:description("Compiles a Swift subset to an LLVM IR module and runs it with the built-in
IR interpreter and the MetaJS handle runtime (llvm.RunJS).

The subset: top level code that runs in source order (declare before use, no
hoisting), let/var declarations with an optional type annotation and an
optional initializer (types are parsed and ignored, let is not enforced, and an
uninitialized declaration starts as nil), functions with LABELLED parameters
(func greet(name: String, from town: String) -> String, called greet(name: x,
from: y)), default parameter values, variadic parameters, inout parameters,
@autoclosure, overloading by parameter type, nested functions and nested types,
single expression bodies with an implicit return, struct and class (and actor)
with stored properties, methods and an explicit init (self and implicit
unqualified property access inside methods, construction without new; a struct
without an init gets the memberwise one), if/else (braces required), while,
repeat/while, for-in over the ranges 1...5 (closed) and 1..<5 (half-open), over
arrays and over dictionaries, an optional where clause on a for, labelled loops
with a labelled break/continue, guard, switch over values, break/continue,
closures as values with capture lists, the shorthand arguments dollar-zero and
up and trailing closure call syntax, the array higher order methods map/filter/
forEach plus append/contains/count/first/last, arrays and dictionaries with
subscript read/write and .count, tuples (labelled or not, tuple patterns in let
and in assignment, tuple return types), string interpolation, the nil-coalescing
operator a ?? b, optional chaining a?.b and a?[i], force unwrap a!, nil,
print(...) and return. Optional binding in conditions: if let / guard let /
while let (including the Swift 5.7 shorthand if let x), compound comma
conditions, if case / guard case patterns, a where clause on a binding, and
for case PAT in xs. Int arithmetic is 32 bit and / truncates; + concatenates
when a side is a String; == compares strings by value and objects by identity.
A plain enum of bare cases becomes named string constants, with or without a
conformance list.

Functions, methods, init and closures become IR functions jsf_N(env, args)
(methods and init get the instance prepended and bind both this and self, so
implicit property access resolves through js_kget/js_kset). Classes and structs
become descriptor objects with a __ctor (default property initializers) and an
init closure; construction runs __ctor then init. Method calls dispatch through
js_mcall, subscript through js_pyget/js_pyset, dictionaries through js_dict_new,
and ?? compiles to a null test branching around the right side (a phi merges).
A binding condition compiles to a nil test branching to the clause's failure
block, and a pattern to a chain of such tests. throw calls js_throw and do/catch
compiles each body to a js_closure handed to js_try (Swift has no finally; the
first catch wins, an unbound catch binds `error`). defer compiles the rest of
its block into a js_try whose FINALLY closure is the defer body, so it runs on
the normal path, on a return and on a throw, and nested defers unwind LIFO.
The whole program becomes jsmain(env, args) executed in order.
Conditional compilation (#if / #elseif / #else / #endif, at top level, in a
block, in a type body, in a closure body and around the cases of a switch) is
STRUCTURAL: the condition is read as raw text to the end of its line and never
evaluated, every branch is parsed like ordinary code, and only the first branch
whose condition is not literally false (or 0) is emitted - which for a real
condition such as os(macOS), canImport(Foundation) or swift(>=5.7) is always the
first branch. A declaration made under #if stays visible after the #endif.
#available and #unavailable compile to true and false; #sourceLocation /
#error / #warning / #assert are accepted and ignored, and a leading hashbang
line is skipped.

Not in the subset (accepted structurally and reported as not implemented under
-warn-unsupported, or simply not parsed): floating point (the runtime is 32-bit
integer only), the numeric and string literal forms beyond plain decimals and a
double-quoted string with interpolation, protocols, extensions, generics (parsed
and ignored), enums with raw or associated values, subscript declarations,
computed properties and property observers, lazy and static members, property
wrappers, initializer overloading and failable initializers, inheritance beyond
a parsed superclass name, operator declarations, async/await, as/is casts, typed
catch discrimination and struct value semantics (structs behave like classes).

Top level self checking programs count failures and end with exit(failures).
The same language with the same semantics is interpreted directly by
swift-interpreter.abnf.") ;


// --- main rules

// Shared token productions (languages/lib).
:include("lib/cstyle-comments.abnf") ;
:include("lib/ident.abnf") ;
:include("lib/numbers.abnf") ;
:include("lib/bools.abnf") ;

:startRule(Program) ;
:whitespace(Whitespace) ;

// Top level items become statements of jsmain, emitted in source order.
Program     <~~ buildMain(takeAll()) ~~>
            = [ Hashbang ] { TopItem } ;
TopItem     = PoundIfTop | FunTop | TypeTop | UnsupTop | TopStmt ;
FunTop      <~~ push(makeFunStmt(pop())) ~~> = [ Modifiers ] FunDecl ;
TypeTop     = [ Modifiers ] ( StructDecl | ClassDecl | ActorDecl | EnumDecl ) ;
UnsupTop    = [ Modifiers ] UnsupDecl ;
TopStmt     = Statement ;

// ----- #if / #elseif / #else / #endif conditional compilation -----
// Structural only: the condition is consumed as raw text to the end of its line
// and NOT evaluated. Every branch is parsed like ordinary code (so an unlowered
// construct in an inactive branch is still reported), and exactly one branch is
// emitted: the first whose condition is not the literal `false` / `0`, which for
// a real condition like os(macOS) or canImport(Foo) is always the FIRST branch.
// The kept branch's items are spliced into the enclosing list, so a declaration
// made under #if is visible after the #endif, as in Swift.
PoundIfTop  <~~ var xs = poundPick(takeAll()); for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) { push(xs[i]) } ~~>
            = PoundIf PoundCond PoundBodyTop { PoundElseIf PoundCond PoundBodyTop }
              [ PoundElse PoundBodyTop ] PoundEndif ;
PoundBodyTop <~~ push({branch: takeAll()}) ~~> = { TopItem } ;
// A statement-level #if lives in the item list of a block (and of a switch body),
// not in Statement itself, because it can contribute more than one statement -
// and because Statement wraps exactly one popped thunk in stmtPos.
PoundIfStmt <~~ var xs = poundPick(takeAll()); for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) { push(xs[i]) } ~~>
            = PoundIf PoundCond PoundBodyStmt { PoundElseIf PoundCond PoundBodyStmt }
              [ PoundElse PoundBodyStmt ] PoundEndif ;
PoundBodyStmt <~~ push({branch: takeAll()}) ~~> = { PoundIfStmt | Statement } ;
PoundIfMember <~~ var xs = poundPick(takeAll()); for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) { push(xs[i]) } ~~>
            = PoundIf PoundCond PoundBodyMember { PoundElseIf PoundCond PoundBodyMember }
              [ PoundElse PoundBodyMember ] PoundEndif ;
PoundBodyMember <~~ push({branch: takeAll()}) ~~> = { Member } ;
// A #if around case labels of a switch: its branches hold labels AND statements.
PoundIfCase <~~ var xs = poundPick(takeAll()); for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) { push(xs[i]) } ~~>
            = PoundIf PoundCond PoundBodyCase { PoundElseIf PoundCond PoundBodyCase }
              [ PoundElse PoundBodyCase ] PoundEndif ;
PoundBodyCase <~~ push({branch: takeAll()}) ~~> = { PoundIfCase | CaseLabel | Statement } ;
// A #if inside a closure body, whose items are the {stmt} / {expr} lambda records.
PoundIfLam  <~~ var xs = poundPick(takeAll()); for (var i = 0; i < xs.length; i++) { push(xs[i]) } ~~>
            = PoundIf PoundCond PoundBodyLam { PoundElseIf PoundCond PoundBodyLam }
              [ PoundElse PoundBodyLam ] PoundEndif ;
PoundBodyLam <~~ push({branch: takeAll()}) ~~> = { PoundIfLam | LamStmt } ;
// #elseif is spelled before #else on purpose: as a PEG, "#else" would match the
// prefix of "#elseif" and leave a stray `if` to be read as an if statement.
PoundIf     = "#if" ;
PoundElseIf = "#elseif" ;
PoundElse   <~~ push({pcond: "1"}) ~~> = "#else" ;
PoundEndif  = "#endif" ;
// The condition: every byte up to (not including) the end of the line, with
// whitespace skipping switched off so the run cannot cross the line break.
PoundCond   <~~ push({pcond: up.in}) ~~>
            = :whitespace() { PoundCondChar } :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
PoundCondChar = "\x00"..."\x09" | "\x0b" | "\x0c" | "\x0e"..."\U0010ffff" ;

// #sourceLocation(...) / #error(...) / #warning(...): accepted and ignored.
PoundDirective <~~ push(function(b) { return b }) ~~>
            = PoundDirName SkipParen ;
PoundDirName = "#sourceLocation" | "#error" | "#warning" | "#assert" ;
// The same directives written inside a type body; the class builder ignores the
// empty member record they push, exactly as it ignores deinit's.
MemberDirective <~~ push({}) ~~> = PoundDirName SkipParen ;
// A #! line is only a hashbang on the FIRST line of the file, which is where
// Program matches it.
Hashbang    = "#!" :whitespace() { PoundCondChar } :whitespace(Whitespace) ;

// Declaration modifiers and attributes (@objc, @available(...), @escaping) are
// parsed and ignored.
Modifiers   = { Modifier | Attribute } ;
Attribute   = "@" Id { "." Id } [ SkipParen ] ;
Modifier    = ( "public" | "private" | "fileprivate" | "internal" | "open"
              | "final" | "static" | "mutating" | "nonmutating"
              | "override" | "lazy" | "weak" | "unowned" | "convenience"
              | "required" | "dynamic" | "indirect" | "package"
              | "nonisolated" | "distributed" | "borrowing" | "consuming" ) KwEnd ;
// `class` is a type-member modifier (class var / class func) as well as a
// declaration keyword, so it is NOT in Modifier - a greedy Modifiers would eat the
// `class` of `@objc class Cache { ... }` and leave nothing for ClassDecl. Member
// tries the nested-type alternative first and only then this list.
MemberModifiers = { Modifier | Attribute | ClassMod } ;
ClassMod    = "class" KwEnd ;

// func name(label param: Type, ...) -> Ret { ... }
FunDecl     <~~ push(makeFun(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwFunc Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] ParamList [ FnEffects ] [ "->" AnnType ] [ GenWhere ] FnBody ;

// A function/method/init body. Swift returns the value of a body that is a SINGLE
// expression without writing `return`, so the one-expression form is tried first;
// anything else is an ordinary block. ExprBody is ordered first on purpose - a body
// that starts with a declaration or a `return` fails it immediately.
FnBody      = ExprBody | Block ;
ExprBody    <~~ push(makeExprBody(pop())) ~~>
            = "{" Expression "}" ;
FnEffects   = { ( "throws" | "rethrows" | "async" ) KwEnd } ;
// A generic constraint clause on a function/type: where T: P, U == V (ignored).
GenWhere    = KwWhere GenConstraint { "," GenConstraint } ;
GenConstraint = Type ( ":" TypeList | "==" Type | "=" Type ) ;

ParamList   <~~ push({params: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "(" [ Param { "," Param } ] ")" ;
// A parameter is [externalLabel] internalName : Type; the last identifier binds.
// With two identifiers the first is the ARGUMENT LABEL and the second the bound
// name; with one, the label and the name are the same. The label `_` means "no
// label". The declared type is kept as text, for picking between overloads.
Param       <~~ push(makeParam(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push({pid: up.in}) ~~> [ Id <~~ push({pid: up.in}) ~~> ] ":" [ ParamInout ] { ParamAttr } ParamType [ ParamVariadic ] [ "=" ParamDflt ] ;
ParamInout  <~~ push({pinout: 1}) ~~> = "inout" KwEnd ;
ParamType   <~~ push({ptype: up.in}) ~~> = Type ;
ParamVariadic <~~ push({pvar: 1}) ~~> = "..." ;
ParamDflt   <~~ push({pdflt: pop()}) ~~> = Expression ;
// Parameter/type attributes (@escaping, @autoclosure) take no argument list here,
// so no SkipParen: the ( ... ) that follows belongs to a function type.
ParamAttr   = "@" Id <~~ push({pattr: up.in}) ~~> { "." Id } ;

// class / struct with stored properties, methods and an explicit init.
StructDecl  <~~ push(makeClassStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwStruct Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] "{" { Member } "}" ;
ClassDecl   <~~ push(makeClassStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwClass Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] "{" { Member } "}" ;
// An actor is a class with an isolation domain. There is no executor in this
// runtime (async functions are defined, never awaited), so it lowers like a class.
ActorDecl   <~~ push(makeClassStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwActor Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] "{" { Member } "}" ;
KwActor     = "actor" KwEnd ;
TypeList    = Type { "," Type } ;

// A nested type is matched BEFORE the modifier-led members, so the `class` of
// `class Inner {}` is read as the declaration keyword and the `class` of
// `class var kind` as a modifier (ClassDecl fails on the `var` that follows).
Member      = PoundIfMember | MemberDirective | MemberType | [ MemberModifiers ] ( InitDecl | DeinitDecl | SubscriptDecl | MethodDecl | ComputedProp | PropDecl ) ;
// The nested declaration's own statement is dropped: a nested type is accepted
// structurally, not yet reachable as Outer.Inner.
MemberType  <~~ pop(); push({}) ~~>
            = [ Modifiers ] ( StructDecl | ClassDecl | ActorDecl | EnumDecl | TypeAliasDecl ) ;
InitDecl    <~~ push({method: makeInit(takeAll())}) ~~>
            = KwInit [ "?" | "!" ] [ SkipAngle ] ParamList [ FnEffects ] [ GenWhere ] FnBody ;
// deinit and subscript are accepted structurally, not implemented; a class/struct
// builder ignores the {} marker they push.
// deinit is accepted and ignored - this runtime is garbage collected, so there is
// no deterministic point at which to run it.
DeinitDecl  <~~ push({}) ~~> = KwDeinit SkipBlock ;
SubscriptDecl <~~ notImpl("subscript", up.pos); push({}) ~~>
            = KwSubscript [ SkipAngle ] SkipParen [ "->" Type ] SkipBlock ;
MethodDecl  <~~ push({method: makeFun(takeAll())}) ~~>
            = KwFunc Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] ParamList [ FnEffects ] [ "->" AnnType ] [ GenWhere ] FnBody ;
// var w = 2, h = 3 declares two stored properties; each binding pushes its own
// {prop} record, so the type builder sees them in declaration order.
PropDecl    = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd PropBind { "," PropBind } [ ";" ] ;
PropBind    <~~ push(makeProp(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ ":" AnnType ] [ "=" Expression ] ;
// Computed properties and stored properties with willSet/didSet observers.
ComputedProp <~~ push(notImplStmt("computed property or property observer", up.pos)) ~~>
            = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd Id [ ":" Type ] [ "=" DiscardExpr ] SkipBlock ;

// A plain enum of bare cases becomes named string constants.
EnumDecl    = PlainEnum | ComplexEnum ;
PlainEnum   <~~ push(makeEnumStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwEnum Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] "{" { SimpleCase } "}" ;
SimpleCase  = KwCase Id <~~ push({ecase: up.in}) ~~> { "," Id <~~ push({ecase: up.in}) ~~> } [ ";" ] ;
ComplexEnum <~~ push(notImplStmt("enum with raw or associated values", up.pos)) ~~>
            = KwEnum Id [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] SkipBlock ;

// protocol / extension / typealias: accepted structurally, not implemented.
UnsupDecl   = ImportDecl | ProtocolDecl | ExtensionDecl | TypeAliasDecl ;
// import Geom (or a submodule import 'import struct A.B'): the module name is resolved by
// resolveImport - a builtin module (core.stdlibImports) is a no-op, otherwise it maps to a
// project file (Geom -> Geom.swift, A.B -> A/B.swift) whose top-level declarations are
// stashed by buildMain (importDepth > 0) and prepended to jsmain. The submodule kind is
// parsed and dropped. It pushes no statement, so buildMain never sees the import itself.
ImportDecl  <~~ resolveImport(pop(), up.pos) ~~>
            = KwImport [ ImportKind ] ImportPath [ ";" ] ;
ImportPath  <~~ push(stripWs(up.in)) ~~>
            = Id { "." ( Id | "*" ) } ;
ImportKind  = ( "typealias" | "struct" | "class" | "enum" | "protocol"
              | "func" | "let" | "var" | "inout" ) KwEnd ;
ProtocolDecl <~~ push(notImplStmt("protocol", up.pos)) ~~>
            = KwProtocol Id [ SkipAngle ] [ ":" TypeList ] SkipBlock ;
ExtensionDecl <~~ push(notImplStmt("extension", up.pos)) ~~>
            = KwExtension Type [ ":" TypeList ] SkipBlock ;
// typealias: types are parsed and ignored, so an alias needs nothing at run time.
TypeAliasDecl <~~ push(function(b) { return b }) ~~>
            = KwTypealias Id [ SkipAngle ] "=" Type [ ";" ] ;

// Types are parsed and ignored: arrays [T], dictionaries [K: V], optionals T?,
// implicitly unwrapped T!, tuples/function types (A, B) -> C, dotted and generic,
// opaque/existential `some P` / `any P`, and compositions P & Q. The `&` of a
// composition is spelled ( "&" !"&" ) so `x is T && y` is not read as `T & (&y)`.
Type        = TypeMod TypeSuffixed { TypeAmp TypeMod TypeSuffixed } ;
// The optional / implicitly-unwrapped marker has to be ADJACENT to the type:
// `x is T ? a : b` must keep its conditional, and `T?` never has a space in Swift.
TypeSuffixed = TypeCore { NoSpace ( "?" | "!" ) } ;
// A zero-width guard that fails when whitespace (or end of file) is ahead - the
// dialect skips whitespace before each token, so "no space here" has to be asked
// explicitly.
NoSpace     = :script(~~
    (function() {
        var cc = c.peek(0)
        return (cc === 32 || cc === 9 || cc === 10 || cc === 13 || cc < 0)
            ? abnf.newToken("\x01space-follows", 0)
            : undefined
    })()
~~) ;
TypeAmp     = "&" !"&" ;
TypeMod     = { ( "some" | "any" | "inout" | "borrowing" | "consuming" | "each" ) KwEnd } ;
TypeCore    = "[" Type [ ":" Type ] "]"
            | "(" [ TupleTypeElem { "," TupleTypeElem } ] ")" [ TypeEffects ] [ "->" Type ]
            | Id [ SkipAngle ] { "." Id [ SkipAngle ] } ;
TupleTypeElem = [ TupleTypeLabel ] { ParamAttr } Type [ "..." ] ;
TupleTypeLabel = Id [ Id ] ":" ;

// The element names of a tuple live in its TYPE, not in the literal: for
//     let pair: (n: String, v: Int) = ("k", 9)
// pair.n has to work. AnnType is Type with that one extra job - when the
// annotation is a tuple type whose first element is labelled it pushes the label
// list, and the declaration (or the function return) copies those names onto the
// value. NotArrow declines a function type, whose parameter labels name nothing.
AnnType     = LabelledTupleType | Type ;
LabelledTupleType <~~ push({tlabels: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "(" LtNamed { "," LtElem } ")" NotArrow ;
LtElem      = LtNamed | LtAnon ;
LtNamed     = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> ":" Type ;
LtAnon      <~~ push("") ~~> = Type ;
NotArrow    = !"->" ;
TypeEffects = { ( "async" | "throws" | "rethrows" ) KwEnd } ;

// Every statement production pushes exactly one thunk: function(block) -> block.
// do/throw are genuinely lowered (try/catch via js_try, throw via js_throw); the
// Cplx* / Local* / defer / fallthrough forms are recognized but not lowered - they
// route to notImplStmt (a warning under -warn-unsupported).
Statement   <~~ push(stmtPos(pop())) ~~>
            = PoundDirective
            | Decl | LocalFunc | LocalType | CplxIf | If | CplxGuard | Guard
            | CplxWhile | While | Repeat | For | Switch | Return | Throw | Break
            | Continue | Fallthrough | Do | Defer | Empty | TupleAssign
            | TrailCallStmt | ExprStmt ;

// `keep11 { 20 }` - a call of a plain function written with one trailing closure and
// no parentheses. It is a STATEMENT form rather than an expression form on purpose:
// as an expression, `cond { ... }` would swallow the block of `if cond { ... }`, and
// PEG never goes back to re-read the condition. Every keyword-led statement is
// matched before this rule, so only a bare `name { ... }` reaches it.
TrailCallStmt <~~ push(exprToStmt(pop())) ~~> = TrailCall [ ";" ] ;
TrailCall   <~~ push(makeCall(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> TrailArg { LabTrail } ;

// A loop (or switch) label: `outer: for ... { ... break outer }`. It is part of the
// loop production rather than a statement of its own, so the builder sees its own
// label and a labelled break/continue can name the loop it leaves.
LoopLabel   = Id <~~ push({lbl: up.in}) ~~> ":" ;

// A nested function or nested type declaration inside a body.
// A nested function declaration inside a body: a closure over the enclosing scope
// bound to its own name (so it can recurse and can capture surrounding locals).
LocalFunc   <~~ push(makeLocalFunStmt(pop())) ~~>
            = [ Modifiers ] FunDecl ;
// A nested type declaration inside a body - the same struct/class/enum productions
// as at the top level, run as a statement of the enclosing body.
LocalType   = StructDecl | ClassDecl | ActorDecl | EnumDecl ;

// do { STMTS } catch [pattern] { STMTS } [catch ...]: genuine try/catch (Swift has NO
// finally). throw calls js_throw (a Go panic the runtime unwinds); each body compiles
// to its own IR closure handed to js_try. The first catch clause wins (patterns are
// parsed but not discriminated). A return/break/continue leaving a try or catch body
// becomes a control signal that excDispatch re-issues in the enclosing frame. A catch
// with no `let NAME` binds the implicit name `error`. Each part is marked so makeTry
// can tell them apart. defer and fallthrough stay not lowered.
Do          <~~ push(makeTry(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwDo TryBody { CatchClause } ;
TryBody     <~~ push({trybody: pop()}) ~~>
            = Block ;
CatchClause <~~ push(makeCatch(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwCatch ( CatchLet | CatchPat ) Block ;
// catch let e / catch let e as T / catch let e where c: bind e (the caught value).
CatchLet    = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ "as" KwEnd Type ] [ KwWhere DiscardExpr ] ;
// catch SomeError / catch .case / catch { }: no `let` binding, so the caught value
// binds to the implicit name `error` (always pushed, so makeCatch binds it).
CatchPat    <~~ push("error") ~~>
            = [ DropPattern ] [ KwWhere DiscardExpr ] ;
// The clause's pattern is parsed but not discriminated yet, so its record is
// dropped and the caught value binds to the implicit `error` either way.
DropPattern <~~ pop() ~~> = Pattern ;
// defer { ... }: everything AFTER it in its block is emitted into a js_try whose
// FINALLY closure is the defer body, so it runs on the normal path, on a return (a
// control signal that excDispatch re-issues) and on a throw (js_try re-panics after
// the finally). Nested defers therefore unwind LIFO.
Defer       <~~ push(makeDefer(pop())) ~~>
            = KwDefer Block ;
Throw       <~~ push(makeThrow(pop())) ~~>
            = KwThrow Expression [ ";" ] ;
Fallthrough <~~ push(notImplStmt("fallthrough", up.pos)) ~~>
            = KwFallthrough [ ";" ] ;

// if / guard / while whose condition uses optional binding (if let x = ...),
// pattern matching (if case ...) or a compound comma condition. Plain boolean
// conditions fall through to If/Guard/While, which stay the cheaper single-test
// forms; a clause reaches here only when it carries a comma or a binding. Each
// condition item is emitted in turn and branches to the failure block; the names a
// binding declares live in a child scope for if/while and, Swift-style, in the
// ENCLOSING scope for guard (whose else branch is expected to leave that scope).
CplxIf      <~~ push(makeCondIf(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwIf CplxCondClause Block [ KwElse ElseBody ] ;
CplxGuard   <~~ push(makeCondGuard(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwGuard CplxCondClause KwElse Block ;
CplxWhile   <~~ push(makeCondWhile(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwWhile CplxCondClause Block ;
// A complex clause requires either a comma (2+ conditions) or a leading binding.
CplxCondClause <~~ push({conds: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = CondItem "," CondItem { "," CondItem } | BindCond { "," CondItem } ;
CondItem    = BindCond | CondExpr ;
CondExpr    <~~ push({cexpr: pop()}) ~~> = Expression ;
BindCond    = OptBind | CaseCond ;
// `if let x = e` and the 5.7 shorthand `if let x` (which rebinds x from itself).
OptBind     <~~ push(makeOptBind(takeAll())) ~~>
            = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd BindPat [ ":" Type ] [ "=" CondInit ] [ PatWhere ] ;
CaseCond    <~~ push(makeCaseCond(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwCase Pattern "=" CondInit [ PatWhere ] ;
CondInit    <~~ push({cinit: pop()}) ~~> = Expression ;
PatWhere    <~~ push({cwhere: pop()}) ~~> = KwWhere Expression ;
BindPat     <~~ push({bnames: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "(" BindName { "," BindName } ")" | BindName ;
BindName    <~~ push(up.in) ~~> = Wildcard | Id ;

// A pattern: `_`, `let x`, `x?` (optional pattern), a tuple of patterns, or an
// enum case - `.busy`, `Load19.busy`, optionally with a sub-pattern argument list.
// A bare identifier is a BINDING when it sits under a `let`/`var` and an enum case
// reference otherwise, so emitMatchCore carries that flag down the tree.
Pattern     <~~ push(makePattern(takeAll())) ~~>
            = PatCore { NoSpace "?" <~~ push({popt: 1}) ~~> } ;
PatCore     = PatLet | PatTuple | PatWild | PatEnum ;
PatLet      <~~ push({plet: pop()}) ~~> = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd Pattern ;
PatTuple    <~~ push({ptup: takeAll()}) ~~> = "(" Pattern { "," Pattern } ")" ;
PatWild     <~~ push({pwild: 1}) ~~> = Wildcard ;
PatEnum     <~~ push(makePatEnum(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ "." <~~ push({pdot: 1}) ~~> ] PatPath [ PatArgs ] ;
PatPath     <~~ push({ppath: stripWs(up.in)}) ~~> = Id { "." Id } ;
PatArgs     <~~ push({pargs: takeAll()}) ~~> = "(" [ PatArg { "," PatArg } ] ")" ;
PatArg      = [ PatArgLabel ] Pattern ;
PatArgLabel = Id ":" ;
Wildcard    = "_" KwEnd ;

Block       <~~ push(makeBlockStmt(takeAll())) ~~>
            = "{" { PoundIfStmt | Statement } "}" ;

Decl        = DeclTuple | DeclPlain ;
DeclPlain   <~~ push(makeDecl(takeAll())) ~~>
            = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ ":" AnnType ] [ "=" Expression ] [ ";" ] ;
// let (a, _, c) = someTuple - a tuple-pattern declaration; _ discards its element.
DeclTuple   <~~ push(makeDeclTuple(takeAll())) ~~>
            = ( "let" | "var" ) KwEnd TupNames [ ":" Type ] "=" Expression [ ";" ] ;
TupNames    <~~ push({tnames: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "(" TupName { "," TupName } ")" ;
TupName     <~~ push(up.in) ~~> = Wildcard | Id ;
// (x, y) = (y, x) - assignment through a tuple pattern (a swap, typically).
TupleAssign <~~ push(makeTupleAssign(takeAll())) ~~>
            = TupNames "=" Expression [ ";" ] ;

If          <~~ push(makeIf(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwIf Expression Block [ KwElse ElseBody ] ;
ElseBody    = Block | CplxIf | If ;

While       <~~ push(makeWhileL(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwWhile Expression Block ;

Repeat      <~~ push(makeRepeat(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwRepeat Block KwWhile Expression [ ";" ] ;

// `for case PAT in xs` filters: only the elements the pattern matches run the body
// (and the pattern's `let` names are bound for that iteration). Tried first - its
// `case` would otherwise be read as the loop variable's name by ForRange/ForList.
For         = ForCase | ForRange | ForList ;
ForCase     <~~ push(makeForCase(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwFor KwCase Pattern KwIn Expression [ ForWhere ] Block ;
ForRange    <~~ push(makeForRange(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwFor ForPat KwIn Expression RangeOp Expression [ ForWhere ] Block ;
RangeOp     = "..." <~~ push({rop: "..."}) ~~>
            | "..<" <~~ push({rop: "..<"}) ~~> ;
ForList     <~~ push(makeForList(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwFor ForPat KwIn Expression [ ForWhere ] Block ;
// The loop variable: a name, _ , or a tuple pattern (for (k, v) in aDictionary).
ForPat      = TupNames | ForName ;
ForName     <~~ push({fname: up.in}) ~~> = Wildcard | Id ;
// for x in xs where COND { ... }: the body runs only for the elements that pass.
ForWhere    <~~ push({fwhere: pop()}) ~~> = KwWhere Expression ;

// guard COND else { ... }: a false condition branches into the else block (which
// normally diverges via return/break/continue); a true condition falls through.
Guard       <~~ push(makeGuard(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwGuard Expression KwElse Block ;

// switch SUBJ { case V1, V2: ...  default: ... } - a chain of == tests, no
// fallthrough. Body parsed FLAT (labels before Statement, a bare 'case' is a valid
// identifier); the builder groups statements under the label they follow. break in
// a case leaves the switch (loop stack), continue reaches the enclosing loop.
Switch      <~~ push(makeSwitch(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ LoopLabel ] KwSwitch SwitchSubj "{" { PoundIfCase | CaseLabel | Statement } "}" ;
SwitchSubj  <~~ push({subj: pop()}) ~~>
            = Expression ;
CaseLabel   <~~ push(makeCaseLabel(takeAll())) ~~>
            = ( KwCase Expression <~~ push({v: pop()}) ~~> { "," Expression <~~ push({v: pop()}) ~~> }
              | KwDefault ) ":" ;

Return      <~~ push(makeReturn(takeAll())) ~~>
            = KwReturn [ Expression ] [ ";" ] ;
Break       <~~ push(makeBreakL(takeAll())) ~~>    = KwBreak [ SameLine BreakLbl ] [ ";" ] ;
Continue    <~~ push(makeContinueL(takeAll())) ~~> = KwContinue [ SameLine BreakLbl ] [ ";" ] ;
BreakLbl    <~~ push({lbl: up.in}) ~~> = Id ;

// A zero-width guard that fails at end of line (a newline or a // comment before the
// next token): the label of `break outer` must start on the SAME line, otherwise a
// bare `break` followed by a statement would swallow that statement's first name.
SameLine    = :script(~~
    (function() {
        var i = 0
        var cc = c.peek(i)
        while (cc === 32 || cc === 9) { i++; cc = c.peek(i) }
        return (cc === 10 || cc === 13 || cc < 0 || (cc === 47 && c.peek(i + 1) === 47))
            ? abnf.newToken("\x01newline-follows", 0)
            : undefined
    })()
~~) ;
Empty       <~~ push(function(b) { return b }) ~~> = ";" ;

ExprStmt    <~~ push(exprToStmt(pop())) ~~>
            = Expression [ ";" ] ;

// Every expression production pushes exactly one thunk: function(block) -> {b, v}.
Expression  = Assignment | Ternary ;
Assignment  <~~ push(makeAssign(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Target ( "+=" | "-=" | "*=" | "/=" | "%=" | "=" ) <~~ push(up.in) ~~> Expression ;

Target      <~~ push(makeTargetRef(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> { "." Id <~~ push({key: up.in}) ~~> | TIndex } ;
TIndex      <~~ push({idx: pop()}) ~~>
            = "[" Expression "]" ;

Ternary     <~~ push(makeTernary(takeAll())) ~~>
            = OrExpr [ "?" Expression ":" Ternary ] ;
OrExpr      <~~ push(makeOrAnd(takeAll(), true)) ~~>
            = AndExpr { "||" AndExpr } ;
AndExpr     <~~ push(makeOrAnd(takeAll(), false)) ~~>
            = EqExpr { "&&" EqExpr } ;
// === / !== compare object identity; the three-character forms are listed first
// so `a === b` is not read as `a == (= b)`.
EqExpr      <~~ push(foldBinary(takeAll())) ~~>
            = RelExpr { ( "===" | "!==" | "==" | "!=" ) <~~ push(up.in) ~~> RelExpr } ;
RelExpr     <~~ push(foldBinary(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Cast { ( "<=" | ">=" | "<" | ">" ) <~~ push(up.in) ~~> Cast } ;
// e as T / e as? T / e as! T / e is T: recognized, routed to notImplExpr. With no
// cast operator it is a pure pass-through (a single item), so byte output is
// unchanged for programs that do not cast.
Cast        <~~ push(makeCast(takeAll(), up.pos)) ~~>
            = Coalesce { CastOp Type } ;
CastOp      <~~ push({cast: 1}) ~~>
            = ( "as" KwEnd [ "?" | "!" ] | "is" KwEnd ) ;
// a ?? b yields a unless it is nil (the nil-coalescing operator; b only runs then).
Coalesce    <~~ push(makeCoalesce(takeAll())) ~~>
            = AddExpr { "??" AddExpr } ;
AddExpr     <~~ push(foldBinary(takeAll())) ~~>
            = MulExpr { ( "+" | "-" ) <~~ push(up.in) ~~> MulExpr } ;
MulExpr     <~~ push(foldBinary(takeAll())) ~~>
            = UnaryExpr { ( "*" | "/" | "%" ) <~~ push(up.in) ~~> UnaryExpr } ;

UnaryExpr   = Neg | Not | TryExpr | Await | CallMember ;
Neg         <~~ push(makeNeg(pop())) ~~>   = "-" UnaryExpr ;
Not         <~~ push(makeNot(pop())) ~~>   = "!" UnaryExpr ;
// try / try? / try! : the prefix is parsed and ignored and the inner expression is
// lowered normally (a throw inside the call unwinds via js_throw regardless).
TryExpr     = ( KwTry [ "?" | "!" ] ) UnaryExpr ;
// await: recognized as a prefix, routed to notImplExpr.
Await       <~~ pop(); push(notImplExpr("await expression", up.pos)) ~~>
            = KwAwait UnaryExpr ;

CallMember  <~~ push(foldCallMember(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Primary { OptSfx | ForceSfx | MethodSfx | FieldSfx | TupleSfx | IndexSfx | CallSfx } ;
// x!: force-unwrap. Adjacent, and not the start of a != operator. The "not an =
// next" test has to be a script and cannot be !"=" - a literal in this dialect
// skips leading whitespace, so !"=" in `maybe! == 7` looks PAST the space, finds
// the = of == and rejects a force-unwrap that is perfectly fine.
ForceSfx    <~~ push({kind:"force"}) ~~> = NoSpace "!" NotChar61 ;
// x?.y / x?[i]: optional chaining - a nil anywhere along the chain makes the WHOLE
// chain nil instead of failing. Adjacent, and not the start of ?? or a ternary.
OptSfx      <~~ push({kind:"opt"}) ~~> = NoSpace "?" NotChar63 ;
NotChar61   = :script(~~
    (function() { return (c.peek(0) === 61) ? abnf.newToken("\x01eq-follows", 0) : undefined })()
~~) ;
NotChar63   = :script(~~
    (function() { return (c.peek(0) === 63) ? abnf.newToken("\x01q-follows", 0) : undefined })()
~~) ;
MethodSfx   <~~ push({kind:"mcall", name: popName(), args: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "." Id <~~ push({mname: up.in}) ~~> MArgs ;
FieldSfx    = "." Id <~~ push({kind:"field", name: up.in}) ~~> ;
// t.0 / t.1: a tuple element read. A tuple is an object whose elements live under
// the property names "0", "1", ... (and additionally under their label when the
// element has one), so an element read is an ordinary field read.
TupleSfx    = "." TupleIdx ;
TupleIdx    <~~ push({kind:"field", name: up.in}) ~~>
            = "0"..."9" { "0"..."9" } ;
IndexSfx    <~~ push({kind:"index", idx: pop()}) ~~>
            = "[" Expression "]" ;
// f(args) applied to whatever the chain produced so far - a closure out of an array
// (queued[0]()), a function returned by a function, a computed member. The opening
// paren has to be ADJACENT: `print(x)` on one line and `(a, b) = (b, a)` on the
// next must stay two statements, not a call of the first one's result.
CallSfx     <~~ push({kind:"call", args: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = NoSpaceParen "(" [ CallArg { "," CallArg } ] ")" ;
NoSpaceParen = :script(~~
    (function() {
        return (c.peek(0) === 40) ? undefined : abnf.newToken("\x01space-before-paren", 0)
    })()
~~) ;
MArgs       = "(" [ CallArg { "," CallArg } ] ")" [ TrailArg { LabTrail } ] | TrailArg { LabTrail } ;
// A trailing closure is the callee's last argument; the second and further ones
// carry their argument label (Swift 5.3 multiple trailing closures).
TrailArg    <~~ push(makeTrailArg(pop())) ~~> = Closure ;
LabTrail    <~~ push(makeLabTrail(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push({alabel: up.in}) ~~> ":" Closure ;

// An argument carries its label (matched against the parameter labels of the
// callee, so a call may leave defaulted parameters out) and, for &x, the name it
// passes by reference.
CallArg     <~~ push(makeCallArg(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ ArgLabel ] ( InoutArg | Expression ) ;
ArgLabel    = Id <~~ push({alabel: up.in}) ~~> ":" ;
// &x: an inout argument. Spelled ( "&" !"&" ) so it cannot start on the first
// character of a && operator.
InoutArg    = "&" !"&" Id <~~ push({aref: up.in}) ~~> ;

Primary     = Paren | Template | FloatLit | IntLit | True | False | Nil
            | PoundExpr | Closure | DictLit | ArrayLit | Shorthand | MultiTrail | Call | VarRef ;

// The # expression literals. #available / #unavailable answer a constant (this
// runtime has no platform to compare against, and the guarded code is the code
// we want to run); the rest are recognized and reported as not implemented.
// Longest first: "#file" would otherwise match the front of "#fileID".
PoundExpr   = PoundAvail | PoundUnavail | PoundCallLit | PoundBareLit ;
PoundAvail  <~~ push(makeConst(true)) ~~>  = "#available" SkipParen ;
PoundUnavail <~~ push(makeConst(false)) ~~> = "#unavailable" SkipParen ;
PoundCallLit <~~ push(notImplExpr("# expression", up.pos)) ~~>
            = ( "#selector" | "#keyPath" | "#colorLiteral" | "#imageLiteral"
              | "#fileLiteral" | "#externalMacro" ) SkipParen ;
PoundBareLit <~~ push(notImplExpr("# literal", up.pos)) ~~>
            = ( "#fileID" | "#filePath" | "#file" | "#function" | "#line"
              | "#column" | "#dsohandle" ) KwEnd ;

// ( e ) is a pass-through; ( e, e, ... ) is a tuple, recognized and routed to
// notImplExpr. Element labels (x: e) are accepted and dropped.
Paren       <~~ push(makeParen(takeAll(), up.pos)) ~~>
            = "(" TupleElem { "," TupleElem } ")" ;
TupleElem   <~~ push(makeTupleElem(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ TupleLabel ] Expression ;
TupleLabel  = Id <~~ push({tlabel: up.in}) ~~> ":" ;
// Floating-point literals (3.14): recognized, routed to notImplExpr (the runtime
// is 32-bit integer only). Tried before IntLit; a plain integer or a range (1...5)
// still parses as IntLit because a fractional digit is required.
FloatLit    <~~ push(notImplExpr("floating-point literal", up.pos)) ~~>
            = ( "0" | "1"..."9" ) :whitespace() { "0"..."9" } "." "0"..."9" { "0"..."9" } :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
// Closure shorthand arguments ($0, $1, ...): recognized, routed to notImplExpr.
// Closure shorthand arguments ($0, $1, ...): a closure without a signature binds
// its arguments under exactly these names, so the shorthand is an ordinary read.
Shorthand   = "$" :whitespace() ShortIdx :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
ShortIdx    <~~ push(makeVarRef("$" + up.in)) ~~>
            = "0"..."9" { "0"..."9" } ;

Closure     <~~ push(makeClosure(takeAll())) ~~>
            = "{" [ ClosureSig ] { PoundIfLam | LamStmt } "}" ;
ClosureSig  <~~ push(makeClosureSig(takeAll())) ~~>
            = [ CaptureList ] "(" [ ClParam { "," ClParam } ] ")" [ FnEffects ] [ "->" Type ] KwIn
            | [ CaptureList ] ClParam { "," ClParam } KwIn
            | CaptureList KwIn ;
ClParam     = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ ":" Type ] ;
// { [x, weak y] in ... }: a capture list snapshots the named variables at the
// moment the closure is created.
CaptureList <~~ push({caps: takeAll()}) ~~>
            = "[" [ CapItem { "," CapItem } ] "]" ;
CapItem     = [ CapMode ] Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> [ "=" DiscardExpr ] ;
CapMode     = ( "weak" | "unowned" ) KwEnd ;
LamStmt     = LamCtrl | LamExpr ;
LamCtrl     <~~ push({stmt: pop()}) ~~>
            = Decl | While | Repeat | For | Return | Break | Continue | If ;
LamExpr     <~~ push({expr: pop()}) ~~>
            = Expression [ ";" ] ;

DictLit     <~~ push(makeDict(takeAll())) ~~>
            = "[" ( ":" | DictEntry { "," DictEntry } ) "]" ;
DictEntry   <~~ var v = pop(); push({dk: pop(), dv: v}) ~~>
            = Expression ":" Expression ;
ArrayLit    <~~ push(makeArray(takeAll())) ~~>
            = "[" [ Expression { "," Expression } ] "]" ;

Call        <~~ push(makeCall(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> "(" [ CallArg { "," CallArg } ] ")" [ TrailArg { LabTrail } ] ;
// f { ... } label: { ... }: a call written with two or more trailing closures and no
// parentheses. Only the MULTI-closure form is accepted without parentheses - a bare
// `name { ... }` would make `if cond { ... }` parse as a call of cond.
MultiTrail  <~~ push(makeCall(takeAll())) ~~>
            = Id <~~ push(up.in) ~~> TrailArg LabTrail { LabTrail } ;

// String interpolation: "sum = \(a + b)".
Template    <~~ push(makeTemplate(takeAll())) ~~>
            = '"' :whitespace() { TplExpr | TplChunk } '"' :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
TplExpr     <~~ push({e: pop()}) ~~>
            = "\\(" :whitespace(Whitespace) Expression ")" ;
TplChunk    <~~ push({s: unescapeJs(up.in)}) ~~>
            = TplChar { TplChar } ;
TplChar     = TplEsc | TplPlain ;
TplEsc      = "\\" ( "n" | "t" | "r" | "0" | "\\" | @'"' | "'" ) ;
TplPlain    = "\x20"..."\x21" | "\x23"..."\x5b" | "\x5d"..."\x7e" | @"\t" | "\x7f"..."\U0010ffff" ;

Nil         <~~ push(makeConst(null)) ~~>  = "nil" KwEnd ;
VarRef      <~~ push(makeVarRef(up.in)) ~~> = Id ;

// ----- Widened surface: a balanced { ... } / < ... > run consumed but ignored -----
SkipBlock   = "{" { SkipItem } "}" ;
SkipItem    = SkipStr | SkipChar | SkipBlock | SkipOther ;
SkipStr     = '"' :whitespace() { SkipStrEsc | SkipStrChar } '"' :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
SkipStrEsc  = "\\" "\x00"..."\U0010ffff" ;
SkipStrChar = "\x00"..."\x21" | "\x23"..."\x5b" | "\x5d"..."\U0010ffff" ;
SkipChar    = "'" :whitespace() { SkipChEsc | SkipChChar } "'" :whitespace(Whitespace) ;
SkipChEsc   = "\\" "\x00"..."\U0010ffff" ;
SkipChChar  = "\x00"..."\x26" | "\x28"..."\x5b" | "\x5d"..."\U0010ffff" ;
SkipOther   = "\x00"..."\x21" | "\x23"..."\x26" | "\x28"..."\x7a" | "\x7c" | "\x7e"..."\U0010ffff" ;

SkipAngle   = "<" { SkipAngle | SkipAngleItem } ">" ;
SkipAngleItem = "\x00"..."\x3b" | "\x3d" | "\x3f"..."\U0010ffff" ;

// A balanced ( ... ) run consumed but ignored (attribute args, subscript params).
SkipParen   = "(" { SkipStr | SkipChar | SkipParen | SkipPOther } ")" ;
SkipPOther  = "\x00"..."\x21" | "\x23"..."\x26" | "\x2a"..."\U0010ffff" ;

DiscardExpr <~~ pop() ~~> = Expression ;

KwFunc      = "func" KwEnd ;
KwImport    = "import" KwEnd ;
KwWhere     = "where" KwEnd ;
KwDeinit    = "deinit" KwEnd ;
KwSubscript = "subscript" KwEnd ;
KwDo        = "do" KwEnd ;
KwCatch     = "catch" KwEnd ;
KwDefer     = "defer" KwEnd ;
KwThrow     = "throw" KwEnd ;
KwFallthrough = "fallthrough" KwEnd ;
KwTry       = "try" KwEnd ;
KwAwait     = "await" KwEnd ;
KwStruct    = "struct" KwEnd ;
KwClass     = "class" KwEnd ;
KwEnum      = "enum" KwEnd ;
KwCase      = "case" KwEnd ;
KwInit      = "init" KwEnd ;
KwProtocol  = "protocol" KwEnd ;
KwExtension = "extension" KwEnd ;
KwTypealias = "typealias" KwEnd ;
KwIf        = "if" KwEnd ;
KwGuard     = "guard" KwEnd ;
KwSwitch    = "switch" KwEnd ;
KwDefault   = "default" KwEnd ;
KwElse      = "else" KwEnd ;
KwWhile     = "while" KwEnd ;
KwRepeat    = "repeat" KwEnd ;
KwFor       = "for" KwEnd ;
KwIn        = "in" KwEnd ;
KwReturn    = "return" KwEnd ;
KwBreak     = "break" KwEnd ;
KwContinue  = "continue" KwEnd ;

// ---


:startScript(~~

    // Shared emitter machinery (module, handle constants, externs, loopStack
    // protocol, expression/statement builders); see the `core` knobs below.
    include("lib/compile-core.js")

    var hidCount = 0     // Names hidden loop bounds.
    var classNames = {}  // Known struct/class names (constructor calls).

    function fail(msg) { println("swift compiler error: " + msg); exit(1) }

    // ----- Imports -----
    // System frameworks / modules the platform already provides (the standard library,
    // Foundation and the common Apple frameworks, plus the platform C libraries);
    // importing one is a no-op. Anything else is a project module we resolve to a file.
    core.stdlibImports = ["Swift", "Foundation", "Dispatch", "Combine", "SwiftUI", "UIKit",
                          "AppKit", "CoreGraphics", "CoreData", "CoreFoundation", "ObjectiveC",
                          "Darwin", "Glibc"]

    // Project-file imports: 'import Geom' looks for Geom.swift (a dotted 'import A.B'
    // for A/B.swift, then A.swift) under the program's directory and the -i roots. The
    // file is parsed with this grammar; its top-level declarations are stashed by
    // buildMain (importDepth > 0) and prepended to jsmain. A file is imported once;
    // repeats and cycles are no-ops.
    var importedFiles = {}
    var importDepth = 0
    // imported files top-level items: stashImported / emitImported (compile-core)
    core.importFile = function(path, pos) {
        var rel = path.split(".").join("/")
        var cands = [rel + ".swift"]
        var cut = -1
        for (var k = 0; k < rel.length; k++) { if (rel.charAt(k) == "/") { cut = k } }
        if (cut > 0) { cands.push(rel.substring(0, cut) + ".swift") }
        for (var i = 0; i < cands.length; i++) {
            var file = c.findImport(cands[i])
            if (file == "") { continue }
            if (importedFiles["$" + file] == true) { return true }
            importedFiles["$" + file] = true
            var text = c.readFile(file)
            var asg = c.parse(c.agrammar, text, null, file)
            c.pushSource(file, text)
            importDepth = importDepth + 1
            c.compile(asg)
            importDepth = importDepth - 1
            c.popSource()
            return true
        }
        return false
    }

    // ----- try/catch and throw (Swift has no finally) -----
    // Each do/catch body compiles to its own IR closure handed to js_try (jsrt.go): it
    // runs the try under a Go recover and routes a thrown value to the catch closure (a
    // one-parameter function bound to the catch name). The first catch clause wins.
    // makeCatch is shared - see lib/compile-core.js.
    function makeTry(items) {
        var tryT = anytype, catchT = anytype, catchName = anytype
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            if (items[i].trybody != undefined) { tryT = items[i].trybody }
            else if (items[i].catchbody != undefined) {
                if (catchT == undefined) { catchT = items[i].catchbody; catchName = items[i].catchname }
            }
        }
        return function(b) {
            // The try and catch bodies are ctl closures (isCtl), so a return/break/
            // continue leaving them becomes a control signal that excDispatch re-issues.
            var tryClo = callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(emitFunc([], tryT, false, true)), curScopeV])
            var catchClo = hUndef
            if (catchT != undefined) {
                var cn = (catchName != undefined) ? catchName : "error"
                catchClo = callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(emitFunc([cn], catchT, false, true)), curScopeV])
            }
            // Swift has no finally, so the finally closure is always undefined.
            var ctl = callExt(b, "js_try", [tryClo, catchClo, hUndef])
            return excDispatch(b, ctl)
        }
    }
    // throw e: evaluate e and raise it with js_throw (a Go panic the runtime unwinds).
    function makeThrow(e) {
        return function(b) {
            var r = e(b)
            callExt(r.b, "js_throw", [r.v])
            r.b.NewRet(hUndef) // Never reached: js_throw unwinds on the host side.
            return deadBlock()
        }
    }

    // ----- Expression thunks: function(block) -> {b, v} -----

    // e as/as?/as! T and e is T carry a {cast:1} marker per operator. With no
    // marker the single operand thunk passes through unchanged; a cast is not
    // lowered (the runtime has no dynamic types), so it becomes a placeholder.
    function makeCast(items, pos) {
        if (items.length == 1) { return items[0] }
        return notImplExpr("type cast (as / is)", pos)
    }

    // ----- Tuples -----
    // A tuple is a plain object carrying its elements under the property names
    // "0", "1", ... plus, for a labelled element, under its label - so t.0 and
    // t.lo are both ordinary js_get reads and the runtime needs no new type.
    function makeTupleElem(items) {
        if (items.length > 1) { return {lbl: items[0].tlabel, t: items[1]} }
        return {lbl: null, t: items[0]}
    }
    // ( e ) passes the single unlabelled operand through; anything else is a tuple.
    function makeParen(items, pos) {
        if (items.length == 1 && items[0].lbl == null) { return items[0].t }
        return function(b) {
            var t = callExt(b, "js_obj_new", [])
            callExt(b, "js_set", [t, emitStr(b, "__tuple"), emitNum(b, items.length)])
            for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                var r = items[i].t(b)
                b = r.b
                callExt(b, "js_set", [t, emitStr(b, "" + i), r.v])
                if (items[i].lbl != null) { callExt(b, "js_set", [t, emitStr(b, items[i].lbl), r.v]) }
            }
            return {b: b, v: t}
        }
    }
    // Copies the element names of a tuple TYPE onto a tuple value (the names of a
    // tuple live in its type, so `let p: (n: String, v: Int) = ("k", 9)` has to
    // make p.n work).
    function emitRelabel(b, v, labels) {
        for (var i = 0; i < labels.length; i++) {
            if (labels[i] == "") { continue }
            callExt(b, "js_set", [v, emitStr(b, labels[i]), callExt(b, "js_get", [v, emitStr(b, "" + i)])])
        }
        return v
    }
    // let (a, _, c) = t  /  (x, y) = (y, x): bind or assign element by element.
    function makeDeclTuple(items) {
        var names = items[0].tnames
        var init = items[1]
        return function(b) {
            var r = init(b)
            b = r.b
            for (var i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
                if (names[i] == "_") { continue }
                var ev = callExt(b, "js_get", [r.v, emitStr(b, "" + i)])
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, names[i]), ev])
            }
            return b
        }
    }
    function makeTupleAssign(items) {
        var names = items[0].tnames
        var init = items[1]
        return function(b) {
            var r = init(b)
            b = r.b
            for (var i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
                if (names[i] == "_") { continue }
                var ev = callExt(b, "js_get", [r.v, emitStr(b, "" + i)])
                callExt(b, "js_kset", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, names[i]), ev])
            }
            return b
        }
    }

    // A body that is a single expression returns that expression's value.
    function makeExprBody(t) {
        return function(b) {
            var r = t(b)
            var v = retLabelled(r.b, r.v)
            emitInoutBacks(r.b)
            return retStmt(r.b, v)
        }
    }

    // ----- Loop control with labels -----
    // loopStack entries carry the label of their loop (null when unlabelled); a
    // labelled break/continue branches to the named entry rather than the top one.
    function loopFind(lbl) {
        for (var i = loopStack.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (loopStack[i].lbl === lbl) { return loopStack[i] }
        }
        return null
    }
    function makeBreakL(items) {
        if (items.length == 0) { return makeBreak() }
        var lbl = items[0].lbl
        return function(b) {
            var e = loopFind(lbl)
            if (e != null) { b.NewBr(e.brk) } else { emitBreak(b) }
            return deadBlock()
        }
    }
    function makeContinueL(items) {
        if (items.length == 0) { return makeContinue() }
        var lbl = items[0].lbl
        return function(b) {
            var e = loopFind(lbl)
            if (e != null) { b.NewBr(e.cont) } else { emitContinue(b) }
            return deadBlock()
        }
    }
    // Is this value a dictionary? js_keys aborts on a string or a number, so the
    // test has to be "an object that is not an array" rather than a bare js_keys.
    function emitIsDict(bb, v) {
        var isArr = callExt(bb, "js_is_type", [v, emitStr(bb, "Array")])
        var chkB = curF.NewBlock("")
        var joinB = curF.NewBlock("")
        var fromB = bb
        bb.NewCondBr(truthy(bb, isArr), joinB, chkB)
        var isObj = callExt(chkB, "js_seq", [callExt(chkB, "js_typeof", [v]), emitStr(chkB, "object")])
        chkB.NewBr(joinB)
        var phi = joinB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(hFalse, fromB), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(isObj, chkB)])
        return {b: joinB, v: phi}
    }
    function itemLbl(items) {
        if (items.length > 0 && items[0] != undefined && items[0].lbl != undefined) { return items[0].lbl }
        return null
    }
    function itemsAfterLbl(items) {
        if (itemLbl(items) != null) { return items.slice(1) }
        return items
    }
    // Binds one iteration value to the loop pattern (a name, _ or a tuple pattern).
    function emitBindForPat(b, pat, v) {
        if (pat.tnames != undefined) {
            for (var i = 0; i < pat.tnames.length; i++) {
                if (pat.tnames[i] == "_") { continue }
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, pat.tnames[i]),
                                             callExt(b, "js_get", [v, emitStr(b, "" + i)])])
            }
            return
        }
        if (pat.fname != "_") { callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, pat.fname), v]) }
    }

    // ----- defer -----
    // A defer is not a statement thunk but a MARKER in its block's item list; the
    // block builder below wraps the rest of the block in a js_try with the defer body
    // as its finally clause. A defer that was never reached - an early return above
    // it - never runs, exactly like Swift's.
    function makeDefer(t) { return {isdefer: t} }
    function swSeqWithDefers(items) {
        var cut = -1
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length && cut < 0; i++) {
            if (typeof items[i] != "function") { cut = i }
        }
        if (cut < 0) { return makeSeq(items) }
        var before = makeSeq(items.slice(0, cut))
        var deferT = items[cut].isdefer
        var restT = swSeqWithDefers(items.slice(cut + 1))
        return function(b) {
            b = before(b)
            // The rest of the block is a ctl closure (isCtl), so a return/break/
            // continue leaving it becomes a signal that excDispatch re-issues here.
            var bodyClo = callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(emitFunc([], restT, false, true)), curScopeV])
            var finClo = callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(emitFunc([], deferT, false, false)), curScopeV])
            return excDispatch(b, callExt(b, "js_try", [bodyClo, hUndef, finClo]))
        }
    }
    // Both overridden by ASSIGNMENT (see the include-override trap in the gotchas doc).
    makeBlockStmt = function(items) {
        var seq = swSeqWithDefers(items)
        return function(b) {
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            b = seq(b)
            curScopeV = saved
            return b
        }
    }
    // A defer marker is a RECORD, not a thunk, so the source-position wrapper the
    // Statement rule applies (active only under -trace / -cfgraph) has to pass it
    // through untouched for the block builder to still recognize it.
    var coreStmtPos = stmtPos
    stmtPos = function(t) {
        if (typeof t != "function") { return t }
        return coreStmtPos(t)
    }

    // ----- Patterns and binding conditions -----
    // A pattern is {opt: n, core: k}: n trailing `?` (an optional pattern, which
    // fails on nil and matches the unwrapped value) around one core form.
    function makePattern(items) {
        var n = 0
        for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) { n++ }
        return {opt: n, core: items[0]}
    }
    // [ "." ] path [ ( subpatterns ) ] - an enum case reference, or (under a `let`)
    // a plain name to bind.
    function makePatEnum(items) {
        var dot = false
        var path = ""
        var args = null
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            if (items[i].pdot != undefined) { dot = true }
            else if (items[i].ppath != undefined) { path = items[i].ppath }
            else if (items[i].pargs != undefined) { args = items[i].pargs }
        }
        return {pdot: dot, ppath: path, pargs: args}
    }
    // A nil / undefined test that branches to failB; returns the block to carry on in.
    function emitNotNil(b, v, failB) {
        var okB = curF.NewBlock("")
        var midB = curF.NewBlock("")
        b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_seq", [v, hNull])), failB, midB)
        midB.NewCondBr(truthy(midB, callExt(midB, "js_seq", [v, hUndef])), failB, okB)
        return okB
    }
    // Emits the test chain of one pattern. On a match control reaches the returned
    // block with every `let`/`var` name of the pattern declared in curScopeV; on a
    // mismatch it branches to failB. binding says a bare identifier names a new
    // variable rather than an enum case.
    function emitMatchPat(b, p, v, binding, failB) {
        if (p.opt > 0) { b = emitNotNil(b, v, failB) }
        return emitMatchCore(b, p.core, v, binding, failB)
    }
    function emitMatchCore(b, k, v, binding, failB) {
        if (k.pwild != undefined) { return b }
        if (k.plet != undefined) { return emitMatchPat(b, k.plet, v, true, failB) }
        if (k.ptup != undefined) {
            var subs = k.ptup
            for (var i = 0; i < subs.length; i++) {
                b = emitMatchPat(b, subs[i], callExt(b, "js_get", [v, emitStr(b, "" + i)]), binding, failB)
            }
            return b
        }
        var simple = !k.pdot && k.pargs == null && k.ppath.indexOf(".") < 0
        if (binding && simple) {
            if (k.ppath != "_") { callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, k.ppath), v]) }
            return b
        }
        // A plain enum's cases are named string constants, so a case pattern is an
        // equality test against that constant; `.name` (leading dot) has no type to
        // resolve against and compares the case NAME directly. A case that carries
        // associated values has no runtime payload yet, so it never matches.
        if (k.pargs != null && k.pargs.length > 0) {
            b.NewBr(failB)
            return curF.NewBlock("")
        }
        var okB = curF.NewBlock("")
        b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_seq", [v, emitStr(b, patCaseName(k))])), okB, failB)
        return okB
    }
    function patCaseName(k) {
        var path = k.ppath
        var cut = -1
        for (var i = 0; i < path.length; i++) { if (path.charAt(i) == ".") { cut = i } }
        return cut < 0 ? path : path.substring(cut + 1)
    }

    // A condition list of if/guard/while: {cexpr} tests, {bindNames} optional
    // bindings and {pat} case patterns, each optionally followed by a where guard.
    // Every item must pass; anything that fails branches to failB.
    function emitConds(b, conds, failB) {
        for (var i = 0; i < conds.length; i++) {
            var cd = conds[i]
            if (cd.cexpr != undefined) {
                var r = cd.cexpr(b)
                b = r.b
                var nb = curF.NewBlock("")
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, r.v), nb, failB)
                b = nb
            } else if (cd.bindNames != undefined) {
                var ri = cd.init(b)
                b = emitNotNil(ri.b, ri.v, failB)
                var ns = cd.bindNames
                if (ns.length == 1) {
                    if (ns[0] != "_") { callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, ns[0]), ri.v]) }
                } else {
                    for (var j = 0; j < ns.length; j++) {
                        if (ns[j] == "_") { continue }
                        callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, ns[j]),
                                                     callExt(b, "js_get", [ri.v, emitStr(b, "" + j)])])
                    }
                }
            } else {
                var rp = cd.init(b)
                b = emitMatchPat(rp.b, cd.pat, rp.v, false, failB)
            }
            if (cd.whereT != null) {
                var rw = cd.whereT(b)
                b = rw.b
                var nb2 = curF.NewBlock("")
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, rw.v), nb2, failB)
                b = nb2
            }
        }
        return b
    }
    function makeOptBind(items) {
        var names = items[0].bnames
        var initT = null
        var whereT = null
        for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) {
            if (items[i].cinit != undefined) { initT = items[i].cinit }
            else if (items[i].cwhere != undefined) { whereT = items[i].cwhere }
        }
        // `if let x` (Swift 5.7) rebinds x from the x already in scope.
        if (initT == null) { initT = makeVarRef(names[0]) }
        return {bindNames: names, init: initT, whereT: whereT}
    }
    function makeCaseCond(items) {
        var initT = null
        var whereT = null
        for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) {
            if (items[i].cinit != undefined) { initT = items[i].cinit }
            else if (items[i].cwhere != undefined) { whereT = items[i].cwhere }
        }
        return {pat: items[0], init: initT, whereT: whereT}
    }
    function makeCondIf(items) {
        var conds = items[0].conds
        var thenT = items[1]
        var elseT = items.length > 2 ? items[2] : null
        return function(b) {
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            var elseB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var contB = curF.NewBlock("")
            thenT(emitConds(b, conds, elseB)).NewBr(contB)
            curScopeV = saved
            if (elseT != null) { elseT(elseB).NewBr(contB) } else { elseB.NewBr(contB) }
            return contB
        }
    }
    // guard binds into the scope it stands in (the bindings outlive the statement);
    // the else block runs only when the clause fails and normally diverges.
    function makeCondGuard(items) {
        var conds = items[0].conds
        var elseT = items[1]
        return function(b) {
            var elseB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var contB = curF.NewBlock("")
            emitConds(b, conds, elseB).NewBr(contB)
            elseT(elseB).NewBr(contB)
            return contB
        }
    }
    function makeCondWhile(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var conds = rest[0].conds
        var bodyT = rest[1]
        return function(b) {
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            var headB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(headB)
            var bodyB = emitConds(headB, conds, exitB)
            loopStack.push({cont: headB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            bodyT(bodyB).NewBr(headB)
            loopStack.pop()
            curScopeV = saved
            return exitB
        }
    }
    // items = [{lbl}?, pattern, listT, {fwhere}?, bodyT] - for case PAT in xs.
    function makeForCase(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var pat = rest[0]
        var listT = rest[1]
        var k = 2
        var whereT = null
        if (rest[k] != undefined && rest[k].fwhere != undefined) { whereT = rest[k].fwhere; k++ }
        var bodyT = rest[k]
        return function(b) {
            hidCount++
            var iName = "$i" + hidCount
            var sName = "$s" + hidCount
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            var r = listT(b)
            b = r.b
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, sName), r.v])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, iName), emitNum(b, 0)])
            var headB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var bodyB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var postB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(headB)
            var iV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, iName)])
            var sV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, sName)])
            var lenV = callExt(headB, "js_pylen", [sV])
            headB.NewCondBr(truthy(headB, callExt(headB, "js_lt", [iV, lenV])), bodyB, exitB)
            var iV2 = callExt(bodyB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(bodyB, iName)])
            var sV2 = callExt(bodyB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(bodyB, sName)])
            var elV = callExt(bodyB, "js_pyget", [sV2, iV2])
            var innerB = emitMatchPat(bodyB, pat, elV, false, postB)
            loopStack.push({cont: postB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            if (whereT != null) {
                var rw = whereT(innerB)
                var runB = curF.NewBlock("")
                rw.b.NewCondBr(truthy(rw.b, rw.v), runB, postB)
                innerB = runB
            }
            bodyT(innerB).NewBr(postB)
            loopStack.pop()
            var iV3 = callExt(postB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, iName)])
            callExt(postB, "js_scope_set", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, iName),
                                            callExt(postB, "js_jadd", [iV3, emitNum(postB, 1)])])
            postB.NewBr(headB)
            curScopeV = saved
            return exitB
        }
    }

    // cond ? a : b -> a diamond with a phi merge (like an if expression).
    function makeTernary(items) {
        if (items.length == 1) { return items[0] }
        var condT = items[0]
        var thenT = items[1]
        var elseT = items[2]
        return function(b) {
            var r = condT(b)
            var thenB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var elseB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var mergeB = curF.NewBlock("")
            r.b.NewCondBr(truthy(r.b, r.v), thenB, elseB)
            var rt = thenT(thenB)
            rt.b.NewBr(mergeB)
            var re = elseT(elseB)
            re.b.NewBr(mergeB)
            var phi = mergeB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(rt.v, rt.b), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(re.v, re.b)])
            return {b: mergeB, v: phi}
        }
    }

    // a ?? b: the right side runs only in its own block when a is nil (phi merge).
    function makeCoalesce(items) {
        if (items.length == 1) { return items[0] }
        return function(b) {
            var r = items[0](b)
            b = r.b
            var v = r.v
            for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) {
                var rightB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var mergeB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var isNull = callExt(b, "js_seq", [v, hNull])
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, isNull), rightB, mergeB)
                var r2 = items[i](rightB)
                r2.b.NewBr(mergeB)
                var phi = mergeB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(v, b), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(r2.v, r2.b)])
                b = mergeB
                v = phi
            }
            return {b: b, v: v}
        }
    }

    function makeArray(items) {
        return function(b) {
            var arrV = callExt(b, "js_arr_new", [])
            for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                var r = items[i](b)
                b = r.b
                callExt(b, "js_arr_push", [arrV, r.v])
            }
            return {b: b, v: arrV}
        }
    }
    function makeDict(items) {
        return function(b) {
            var d = callExt(b, "js_dict_new", [])
            for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                var rk = items[i].dk(b)
                b = rk.b
                var rv = items[i].dv(b)
                b = rv.b
                callExt(b, "js_pyset", [d, rk.v, rv.v])
            }
            return {b: b, v: d}
        }
    }

    // .count -> js_pylen (arrays, strings and dicts); other .name -> js_get;
    // [i] -> js_pyget (core.indexExt); .m(args) -> js_mcall.
    core.indexExt = "js_pyget"
    foldCallMember = function(items) {
        if (items.length == 1) { return items[0] }
        var primary = items[0]
        var suffixes = items.slice(1)
        return function(b) {
            var r = primary(b)
            b = r.b
            var cur = r.v
            // Optional chaining: every ?. adds a block that leaves the chain with nil.
            var nilExits = []
            for (var i = 0; i < suffixes.length; i++) {
                var s = suffixes[i]
                if (s.kind == "opt") {
                    var nB = curF.NewBlock("")
                    var c1B = curF.NewBlock("")
                    var contB = curF.NewBlock("")
                    b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_seq", [cur, hNull])), nB, c1B)
                    c1B.NewCondBr(truthy(c1B, callExt(c1B, "js_seq", [cur, hUndef])), nB, contB)
                    nilExits.push(nB)
                    b = contB
                } else if (s.kind == "force") {
                    // Force unwrap: the value is already the unwrapped one here.
                } else if (s.kind == "mcall") {
                    var ea = emitArgRecs(b, s.args)
                    b = ea.b
                    cur = callExt(b, "js_mcall", [cur, emitStr(b, s.name), ea.v])
                    emitWriteBacks(b, ea.boxes)
                } else if (s.kind == "call") {
                    var eac = emitArgRecs(b, s.args)
                    b = eac.b
                    cur = callExt(b, "js_call", [cur, hUndef, eac.v])
                    emitWriteBacks(b, eac.boxes)
                } else if (s.kind == "field") {
                    if (s.name == "count") { cur = callExt(b, "js_pylen", [cur]) }
                    else { cur = callExt(b, "js_get", [cur, emitStr(b, s.name)]) }
                } else {
                    var ir2 = s.idx(b)
                    b = ir2.b
                    cur = callExt(b, core.indexExt, [cur, ir2.v])
                }
            }
            if (nilExits.length == 0) { return {b: b, v: cur} }
            var mergeB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var inc = [llvm.ir.NewIncoming(cur, b)]
            b.NewBr(mergeB)
            for (var k = 0; k < nilExits.length; k++) {
                nilExits[k].NewBr(mergeB)
                inc.push(llvm.ir.NewIncoming(hNull, nilExits[k]))
            }
            return {b: mergeB, v: mergeB.NewPhi(inc)}
        }
    }

    // The closure signature: an optional capture list and the parameter names.
    function makeClosureSig(items) {
        var caps = []
        var names = []
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            if (typeof items[i] == "string") { names.push(items[i]) }
            else if (items[i].caps != undefined) { caps = items[i].caps }
        }
        return {csig: true, caps: caps, cparams: names}
    }
    // An @autoclosure argument becomes a zero-argument closure, so the expression
    // only runs if the callee actually calls it.
    function autoWrap(t) {
        return function(b) {
            var body = function(bb) {
                var r = t(bb)
                r.b.NewRet(r.v)
                return deadBlock()
            }
            var idx = emitFunc([], body, false)
            return {b: b, v: callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(idx), curScopeV])}
        }
    }
    // A closure becomes an IR function closed over the current scope (js_closure);
    // its value is the last expression. A capture list snapshots its names into a
    // scope of their own; a closure with no parameter names binds its arguments
    // under the shorthand names $0..$3.
    function makeClosure(items) {
        var params = []
        var caps = []
        var start = 0
        if (items.length > 0 && items[0] != undefined && items[0].csig != undefined) {
            params = items[0].cparams
            caps = items[0].caps
            start = 1
        }
        if (params.length == 0) { params = ["$0", "$1", "$2", "$3"] }
        var body = items.slice(start)
        var bodyStmt = function(b) {
            var v = hUndef
            for (var k = 0; k < body.length; k++) {
                if (body[k].expr != undefined) {
                    var r = body[k].expr(b)
                    b = r.b
                    v = r.v
                } else {
                    b = body[k].stmt(b)
                    v = hUndef
                }
            }
            b.NewRet(v)
            return deadBlock()
        }
        return function(b) {
            var env = curScopeV
            if (caps.length > 0) {
                env = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
                for (var ci = 0; ci < caps.length; ci++) {
                    callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [env, emitStr(b, caps[ci]),
                                                 callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, caps[ci])])])
                }
            }
            var savedEnv = curScopeV
            curScopeV = env
            var idx = emitFunc(params, bodyStmt, false)
            curScopeV = savedEnv
            return {b: b, v: callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(idx), env])}
        }
    }

    // ----- Calls: argument labels, default values, variadics and inout -----
    // A call site knows the callee's parameter list whenever the callee was declared
    // earlier in the walk (sigReg, filled by every func/init as it is built), so the
    // arguments a call LEAVES OUT because they are defaulted are filled in here, by
    // matching each argument label against the parameter labels in order. Without a
    // signature the arguments stay positional and the callee's own prologue fills the
    // trailing defaults. Mirrors planArgs/swBindArgs in swift-interpreter.abnf.
    var sigReg = {}
    function regSig(name, params) { sigReg["$" + name] = params }
    function lookupSig(name) { return hasOwn(sigReg, "$" + name) ? sigReg["$" + name] : null }
    function hasOwn(o, n) { return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, n) }

    function makeParam(items) {
        var ids = []
        var type = ""
        var isVar = false
        var isInout = false
        var isAuto = false
        var hasDflt = false
        var dflt = null
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            var it = items[i]
            if (it.pid != undefined) { ids.push(it.pid) }
            else if (it.ptype != undefined) { type = stripWs(it.ptype) }
            else if (it.pvar != undefined) { isVar = true }
            else if (it.pinout != undefined) { isInout = true }
            else if (it.pdflt != undefined) { hasDflt = true; dflt = it.pdflt }
            else if (it.pattr != undefined && it.pattr == "autoclosure") { isAuto = true }
        }
        var name = ids[ids.length - 1]
        var label = ids.length > 1 ? ids[0] : name
        if (label == "_") { label = "" }
        return {name: name, label: label, type: type, variadic: isVar, auto: isAuto,
                inout: isInout, hasDefault: hasDflt, dflt: dflt}
    }
    function pName(p) { return (typeof p == "string") ? p : p.name }
    function makeCallArg(items) {
        var lbl = null
        var t = null
        var ref = null
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            var it = items[i]
            if (typeof it == "function") { t = it }
            else if (it.alabel != undefined) { lbl = it.alabel }
            else if (it.aref != undefined) { ref = it.aref }
        }
        return {lbl: lbl, t: t, ref: ref, dflt: null}
    }
    function makeTrailArg(t) { return {lbl: null, t: t, ref: null, dflt: null} }
    function makeLabTrail(items) { return {lbl: items[0].alabel, t: items[1], ref: null, dflt: null} }

    function planArgs(name, recs) {
        var params = lookupSig(name)
        if (params == null) { return recs }
        var out = []
        var ai = 0
        for (var p = 0; p < params.length; p++) {
            var prm = params[p]
            if (prm.variadic) { break }
            var take = false
            if (ai < recs.length) {
                var l = recs[ai].lbl
                take = (l == null || l == "" || l == prm.label)
            }
            if (take) {
                var rec = recs[ai]
                if (prm.auto && rec.t != null) { rec = {lbl: rec.lbl, t: autoWrap(rec.t), ref: null, dflt: null} }
                out.push(rec)
                ai++
            }
            else if (prm.hasDefault) { out.push({lbl: null, t: null, ref: null, dflt: prm.dflt}) }
        }
        while (ai < recs.length) { out.push(recs[ai]); ai++ }
        return out
    }
    // Emits the argument array. An &x argument becomes a one-slot box the callee
    // writes back into; emitWriteBacks copies the boxes home after the call.
    function emitArgRecs(b, recs) { return emitArgRecsInto(b, recs, null) }
    function emitArgRecsInto(b, recs, into) {
        var arr = (into == null) ? callExt(b, "js_arr_new", []) : into
        var boxes = []
        for (var i = 0; i < recs.length; i++) {
            var v
            if (recs[i].ref != null) {
                var box = callExt(b, "js_obj_new", [])
                callExt(b, "js_set", [box, emitStr(b, "__ref"), emitNum(b, 1)])
                callExt(b, "js_set", [box, emitStr(b, "v"),
                                      callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, recs[i].ref)])])
                v = box
                boxes.push({name: recs[i].ref, box: box})
            } else if (recs[i].dflt != null) {
                var rd = recs[i].dflt(b)
                b = rd.b
                v = rd.v
            } else {
                var r = recs[i].t(b)
                b = r.b
                v = r.v
            }
            callExt(b, "js_arr_push", [arr, v])
        }
        return {b: b, v: arr, boxes: boxes}
    }
    function emitWriteBacks(b, boxes) {
        for (var i = 0; i < boxes.length; i++) {
            callExt(b, "js_kset", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, boxes[i].name),
                                   callExt(b, "js_get", [boxes[i].box, emitStr(b, "v")])])
        }
    }

    // f(args): a struct/class constructor (known at compile time) or a function value.
    function makeCall(items) {
        var name = items[0]
        var args = planArgs(name, items.slice(1))
        return function(b) {
            if (classNames[name] == 1) {
                var clsV = callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name)])
                var objV = callExt(b, "js_obj_new", [])
                callExt(b, "js_set", [objV, emitStr(b, "__class"), clsV])
                // __ctor(this) sets default valued properties.
                var ctorArgs = callExt(b, "js_arr_new", [])
                callExt(b, "js_arr_push", [ctorArgs, objV])
                var ctorV = callExt(b, "js_get", [clsV, emitStr(b, "__ctor")])
                callExt(b, "js_call", [ctorV, hUndef, ctorArgs])
                // init(this, args)
                var initArgs = callExt(b, "js_arr_new", [])
                callExt(b, "js_arr_push", [initArgs, objV])
                var eai = emitArgRecsInto(b, args, initArgs)
                b = eai.b
                var initV = callExt(b, "js_get", [clsV, emitStr(b, "init")])
                callExt(b, "js_call", [initV, hUndef, initArgs])
                emitWriteBacks(b, eai.boxes)
                return {b: b, v: objV}
            }
            var fV = callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name)])
            var ea = emitArgRecs(b, args)
            b = ea.b
            var rv = callExt(b, "js_call", [fV, hUndef, ea.v])
            emitWriteBacks(b, ea.boxes)
            return {b: b, v: rv}
        }
    }

    // Assignment: a plain name goes through js_kget/js_kset (locals, then the
    // properties of self); a .field path targets js_get/js_set; an [i] path
    // targets js_pyget/js_pyset (arrays and dictionaries).
    function emitRefPath(b, ref) {
        var o = callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, ref.name)])
        for (var i = 0; i < ref.path.length - 1; i++) {
            var s = ref.path[i]
            if (s.key != undefined) { o = callExt(b, "js_get", [o, emitStr(b, s.key)]) }
            else { var ri = s.idx(b); b = ri.b; o = callExt(b, "js_pyget", [o, ri.v]) }
        }
        var last = ref.path[ref.path.length - 1]
        if (last.key != undefined) { return {b: b, obj: o, key: emitStr(b, last.key), isField: true} }
        var kr = last.idx(b)
        return {b: kr.b, obj: o, key: kr.v, isField: false}
    }
    function makeAssign(items) {
        var ref = items[0]
        var op = items[1]
        var valT = items[2]
        return function(b) {
            var r = valT(b)
            b = r.b
            var v = r.v
            if (ref.path.length == 0) {
                var nameV = emitStr(b, ref.name)
                if (op != "=") {
                    var old = callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, nameV])
                    v = emitBin(b, op, old, v)
                }
                callExt(b, "js_kset", [curScopeV, nameV, v])
            } else {
                var p = emitRefPath(b, ref)
                b = p.b
                if (p.isField) {
                    if (op != "=") {
                        var oldf = callExt(b, "js_get", [p.obj, p.key])
                        v = emitBin(b, op, oldf, v)
                    }
                    callExt(b, "js_set", [p.obj, p.key, v])
                } else {
                    if (op != "=") {
                        var oldm = callExt(b, "js_pyget", [p.obj, p.key])
                        v = emitBin(b, op, oldm, v)
                    }
                    callExt(b, "js_pyset", [p.obj, p.key, v])
                }
            }
            return {b: b, v: v}
        }
    }

    // items = [{s: chunk} | {e: thunk}...] -> js_jadd fold starting from "".
    function makeTemplate(items) {
        return function(b) {
            var v = emitStr(b, "")
            for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
                var pv
                if (items[i].s != undefined) { pv = emitStr(b, items[i].s) }
                else {
                    var r = items[i].e(b)
                    b = r.b
                    pv = r.v
                }
                v = callExt(b, "js_jadd", [v, pv])
            }
            return {b: b, v: v}
        }
    }

    // ----- Statement thunks: function(block) -> block -----

    // items = [name, {tlabels}?, initThunk]
    function makeDecl(items) {
        var name = items[0]
        var labels = null
        var k = 1
        if (items[k] != undefined && items[k].tlabels != undefined) { labels = items[k].tlabels; k++ }
        var init = items[k]
        // `let v: Int` with no initializer declares the name as nil; the value
        // arrives by a later assignment (Swift's definite-initialization rule is
        // a type-checker job, and this front end does not enforce it).
        if (init == undefined) {
            return function(b) {
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name), hNull])
                return b
            }
        }
        return function(b) {
            var r = init(b)
            b = r.b
            var v = r.v
            if (labels != null) { v = emitRelabel(b, v, labels) }
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name), v])
            return b
        }
    }
    // items = [{lbl}?, condT, bodyT]
    function makeWhileL(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var condT = rest[0]
        var bodyT = rest[1]
        return function(b) {
            var headB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var bodyB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(headB)
            var r = condT(headB)
            r.b.NewCondBr(truthy(r.b, r.v), bodyB, exitB)
            loopStack.push({cont: headB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            bodyT(bodyB).NewBr(headB)
            loopStack.pop()
            return exitB
        }
    }
    // items = [{lbl}?, bodyT, condT] - repeat { ... } while COND
    function makeRepeat(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var bodyT = rest[0]
        var condT = rest[1]
        return function(b) {
            var bodyB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var condB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(bodyB)
            loopStack.push({cont: condB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            bodyT(bodyB).NewBr(condB)
            loopStack.pop()
            var r = condT(condB)
            r.b.NewCondBr(truthy(r.b, r.v), bodyB, exitB)
            return exitB
        }
    }
    // items = [{lbl}?, pat, fromT, {rop}, toT, {fwhere}?, bodyT]. ..< subtracts one.
    function makeForRange(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var pat = rest[0]
        var fromT = rest[1]
        var rop = rest[2].rop
        var toT = rest[3]
        var k = 4
        var whereT = null
        if (rest[k] != undefined && rest[k].fwhere != undefined) { whereT = rest[k].fwhere; k++ }
        var bodyT = rest[k]
        var name = (pat.fname != undefined) ? pat.fname : "$_"
        return function(b) {
            hidCount++
            var tName = "$to" + hidCount
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            var rf = fromT(b)
            b = rf.b
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name), rf.v])
            var rt = toT(b)
            b = rt.b
            var boundV = rt.v
            if (rop == "..<") { boundV = callExt(b, "js_sub", [boundV, emitNum(b, 1)]) }
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, tName), boundV])
            var headB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var bodyB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var postB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(headB)
            var iV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, name)])
            var tV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, tName)])
            headB.NewCondBr(truthy(headB, callExt(headB, "js_le", [iV, tV])), bodyB, exitB)
            loopStack.push({cont: postB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            var innerB = bodyB
            if (whereT != null) {
                var rw = whereT(innerB)
                var runB = curF.NewBlock("")
                rw.b.NewCondBr(truthy(rw.b, rw.v), runB, postB)
                innerB = runB
            }
            bodyT(innerB).NewBr(postB)
            loopStack.pop()
            var iV2 = callExt(postB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, name)])
            callExt(postB, "js_scope_set", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, name), callExt(postB, "js_jadd", [iV2, emitNum(postB, 1)])])
            postB.NewBr(headB)
            curScopeV = saved
            return exitB
        }
    }
    // items = [{lbl}?, pat, listT, {fwhere}?, bodyT]. The sequence walked by index is
    // the array itself, or - for a dictionary - its key array (js_keys); a tuple
    // pattern over a dictionary binds (key, value), like the interpreter.
    function makeForList(items) {
        var lbl = itemLbl(items)
        var rest = itemsAfterLbl(items)
        var pat = rest[0]
        var listT = rest[1]
        var k = 2
        var whereT = null
        if (rest[k] != undefined && rest[k].fwhere != undefined) { whereT = rest[k].fwhere; k++ }
        var bodyT = rest[k]
        var wantPair = pat.tnames != undefined
        return function(b) {
            hidCount++
            var iName = "$i" + hidCount
            var aName = "$a" + hidCount
            var sName = "$s" + hidCount
            var saved = curScopeV
            curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [curScopeV])
            var r = listT(b)
            b = r.b
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, aName), r.v])
            // The indexable sequence: the value itself for an array or a string, its
            // key array for a dictionary.
            var rd = emitIsDict(b, r.v)
            b = rd.b
            var arrB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var dictB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var seqB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, rd.v), dictB, arrB)
            arrB.NewBr(seqB)
            var keysV = callExt(dictB, "js_keys", [r.v])
            dictB.NewBr(seqB)
            var seqV = seqB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(r.v, arrB), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(keysV, dictB)])
            b = seqB
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, sName), seqV])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, iName), emitNum(b, 0)])
            var headB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var bodyB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var postB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewBr(headB)
            var iV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, iName)])
            var sV = callExt(headB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(headB, sName)])
            var lenV = callExt(headB, "js_pylen", [sV])
            headB.NewCondBr(truthy(headB, callExt(headB, "js_lt", [iV, lenV])), bodyB, exitB)
            var iV2 = callExt(bodyB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(bodyB, iName)])
            var sV2 = callExt(bodyB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(bodyB, sName)])
            var aV2 = callExt(bodyB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(bodyB, aName)])
            var rawV = callExt(bodyB, "js_pyget", [sV2, iV2])
            var elV = rawV
            if (wantPair) {
                // A tuple pattern over a dictionary iterates (key, value) pairs; over an
                // array the element already IS the tuple.
                var rd2 = emitIsDict(bodyB, aV2)
                bodyB = rd2.b
                var pArrB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var pDictB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var pJoinB = curF.NewBlock("")
                bodyB.NewCondBr(truthy(bodyB, rd2.v), pDictB, pArrB)
                pArrB.NewBr(pJoinB)
                var pairV = callExt(pDictB, "js_obj_new", [])
                callExt(pDictB, "js_set", [pairV, emitStr(pDictB, "__tuple"), emitNum(pDictB, 2)])
                callExt(pDictB, "js_set", [pairV, emitStr(pDictB, "0"), rawV])
                callExt(pDictB, "js_set", [pairV, emitStr(pDictB, "1"), callExt(pDictB, "js_pyget", [aV2, rawV])])
                pDictB.NewBr(pJoinB)
                elV = pJoinB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(rawV, pArrB), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(pairV, pDictB)])
                bodyB = pJoinB
            }
            emitBindForPat(bodyB, pat, elV)
            loopStack.push({cont: postB, brk: exitB, lbl: lbl})
            var innerB = bodyB
            if (whereT != null) {
                var rw2 = whereT(innerB)
                var runB2 = curF.NewBlock("")
                rw2.b.NewCondBr(truthy(rw2.b, rw2.v), runB2, postB)
                innerB = runB2
            }
            bodyT(innerB).NewBr(postB)
            loopStack.pop()
            var iV3 = callExt(postB, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, iName)])
            callExt(postB, "js_scope_set", [curScopeV, emitStr(postB, iName), callExt(postB, "js_jadd", [iV3, emitNum(postB, 1)])])
            postB.NewBr(headB)
            curScopeV = saved
            return exitB
        }
    }
    function makeReturn(items) {
        var t = items.length > 0 ? items[0] : null
        return function(b) {
            var v = hUndef
            if (t != null) {
                var r = t(b)
                b = r.b
                v = retLabelled(b, r.v)
            }
            emitInoutBacks(b)
            return retStmt(b, v) // plain ret, or a control signal when leaving a try body
        }
    }

    // guard COND else BLOCK: a true condition jumps to the continuation, a false one
    // into the else block; the else normally diverges (its trailing branch is dead).
    function makeGuard(items) {
        var condT = items[0]
        var elseT = items[1]
        return function(b) {
            var r = condT(b)
            b = r.b
            var elseB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var contB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, r.v), contB, elseB)
            elseT(elseB).NewBr(contB)
            return contB
        }
    }

    // A case label carries its value thunks (empty for default).
    function makeCaseLabel(items) {
        var vals = []
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) { vals.push(items[i].v) }
        return {isDefault: items.length == 0, vals: vals}
    }
    // items = [{subj}, label or statement thunk...]: the flat item list is regrouped
    // (every statement belongs to the last label). The dispatch compares (js_seq) the
    // subject to each case value in source order; every body branches to the exit (no
    // fallthrough), a break inside a case leaves the switch, continue reaches the loop.
    function makeSwitch(items) {
        var subj = null
        var cases = []
        var cur = null
        var swLbl = itemLbl(items)
        for (var i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
            var it = items[i]
            if (typeof it == "function") {
                if (cur != null) { cur.body.push(it) }
            } else if (it.lbl != undefined) {
                continue
            } else if (it.subj != undefined) {
                subj = it.subj
            } else {
                cur = {isDefault: it.isDefault, vals: it.vals, body: []}
                cases.push(cur)
            }
        }
        return function(b) {
            var subjV = null
            if (subj != null) {
                var rs = subj(b)
                b = rs.b
                subjV = rs.v
            }
            var exitB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var bodyBs = []
            var dfltB = exitB
            for (var i = 0; i < cases.length; i++) {
                bodyBs.push(curF.NewBlock(""))
                if (cases[i].isDefault) { dfltB = bodyBs[i] }
            }
            for (var i = 0; i < cases.length; i++) {
                if (cases[i].isDefault) { continue }
                for (var v = 0; v < cases[i].vals.length; v++) {
                    var rv = cases[i].vals[v](b)
                    b = rv.b
                    var condV = subjV != null ? callExt(b, "js_seq", [subjV, rv.v]) : rv.v
                    var nextB = curF.NewBlock("")
                    b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, condV), bodyBs[i], nextB)
                    b = nextB
                }
            }
            b.NewBr(dfltB)
            var outerCont = loopStack.length > 0 ? loopStack[loopStack.length - 1].cont : null
            loopStack.push({cont: outerCont, brk: exitB, lbl: swLbl})
            for (var i = 0; i < cases.length; i++) {
                var bb = bodyBs[i]
                var body = cases[i].body
                for (var j = 0; j < body.length; j++) { bb = body[j](bb) }
                bb.NewBr(exitB)
            }
            loopStack.pop()
            return exitB
        }
    }

    // ----- Functions, methods and classes -----

    function paramName(items) { return items[items.length - 1] }

    // Every user function/method/init/closure becomes jsf_N(env, args). Instance
    // functions bind arg 0 to both this and self so implicit property access works.
    // isCtl marks a try/catch body closure: a return/break/continue leaving it emits a
    // control signal instead of a ret/br (see compile-core inCtlBody / excDispatch).
    function emitFunc(params, body, isInstance, isCtl, rlabels) {
        funcCount++
        var idx = funcCount
        var f = m.NewFunc("jsf_" + idx, i64, [llvm.ir.NewParam("env", i64), llvm.ir.NewParam("args", i64)])
        var savedF = curF
        var savedScope = curScopeV
        var savedLoops = loopStack
        var savedTag = curFTag
        curF = f
        curFTag = idx
        loopStack = []
        if (isCtl) { ctlEnter(idx) }
        retLabelStack.push(rlabels == undefined ? null : rlabels)
        var b = f.NewBlock("entry")
        curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [f.Params[0]])
        var off = 0
        if (isInstance) {
            var thisV = callExt(b, "js_arg", [f.Params[1], handle(0)])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "this"), thisV])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "self"), thisV])
            off = 1
        }
        // The parameter prologue. A plain closure parameter is a bare name; a
        // function/method parameter is a record that may be variadic, have a default
        // value or be inout (its argument is a one-slot box written back on the way
        // out - see emitInoutBacks, emitted before every ret).
        var inouts = []
        var nargsV = callExt(b, "js_pylen", [f.Params[1]])
        for (var i = 0; i < params.length; i++) {
            var prm = params[i]
            if (typeof prm == "string") {
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, prm),
                                             callExt(b, "js_arg", [f.Params[1], handle(i + off)])])
                continue
            }
            if (prm.variadic) {
                // Collect the remaining arguments into an array.
                var vArr = callExt(b, "js_arr_new", [])
                var vName = "$va" + i
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, vName), emitNum(b, i + off)])
                var vHead = curF.NewBlock("")
                var vBody = curF.NewBlock("")
                var vExit = curF.NewBlock("")
                b.NewBr(vHead)
                var vi = callExt(vHead, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(vHead, vName)])
                vHead.NewCondBr(truthy(vHead, callExt(vHead, "js_lt", [vi, nargsV])), vBody, vExit)
                var vi2 = callExt(vBody, "js_scope_get", [curScopeV, emitStr(vBody, vName)])
                callExt(vBody, "js_arr_push", [vArr, callExt(vBody, "js_kindex", [f.Params[1], vi2])])
                callExt(vBody, "js_scope_set", [curScopeV, emitStr(vBody, vName),
                                                callExt(vBody, "js_jadd", [vi2, emitNum(vBody, 1)])])
                vBody.NewBr(vHead)
                b = vExit
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, prm.name), vArr])
                continue
            }
            var av = callExt(b, "js_arg", [f.Params[1], handle(i + off)])
            if (prm.hasDefault) {
                // The argument may be missing: fall back to the default expression.
                var dB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var jB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var haveB = b
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_le", [nargsV, emitNum(b, i + off)])), dB, jB)
                var rd = prm.dflt(dB)
                rd.b.NewBr(jB)
                var phi = jB.NewPhi([llvm.ir.NewIncoming(av, haveB), llvm.ir.NewIncoming(rd.v, rd.b)])
                b = jB
                av = phi
            }
            if (prm.inout) {
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "$box$" + prm.name), av])
                av = callExt(b, "js_get", [av, emitStr(b, "v")])
                inouts.push(prm.name)
            }
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, prm.name), av])
        }
        inoutStack.push(inouts)
        var endB = body(b)
        emitInoutBacks(endB)
        endB.NewRet(hUndef)
        inoutStack.pop()
        retLabelStack.pop()
        if (isCtl) { ctlLeave() }
        curF = savedF
        curScopeV = savedScope
        loopStack = savedLoops
        curFTag = savedTag
        return idx
    }
    // The default-property initializer: sets the properties that have a default
    // value on this, before init runs.
    function emitCtor(props) {
        funcCount++
        var idx = funcCount
        var f = m.NewFunc("jsf_" + idx, i64, [llvm.ir.NewParam("env", i64), llvm.ir.NewParam("args", i64)])
        var savedF = curF
        var savedScope = curScopeV
        var savedLoops = loopStack
        var savedTag = curFTag
        curF = f
        curFTag = idx
        loopStack = []
        var b = f.NewBlock("entry")
        curScopeV = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [f.Params[0]])
        var thisV = callExt(b, "js_arg", [f.Params[1], handle(0)])
        callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "this"), thisV])
        callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "self"), thisV])
        for (var p = 0; p < props.length; p++) {
            var r = props[p].init(b)
            b = r.b
            callExt(b, "js_set", [thisV, emitStr(b, props[p].prop), r.v])
        }
        b.NewRet(hUndef)
        curF = savedF
        curScopeV = savedScope
        loopStack = savedLoops
        curFTag = savedTag
        return idx
    }
    // items = [name, {params}, {tlabels}?, bodyThunk]
    function makeFun(items) {
        var k = 2
        var labels = null
        if (items[k] != undefined && items[k].tlabels != undefined) { labels = items[k].tlabels; k++ }
        return {name: items[0], params: items[1].params, body: items[k], rlabels: labels}
    }
    // The inout parameters of the function whose body is currently being emitted:
    // their final values are copied back into their caller's boxes before every ret.
    var inoutStack = []
    function emitInoutBacks(b) {
        if (inoutStack.length == 0) { return }
        var names = inoutStack[inoutStack.length - 1]
        for (var i = 0; i < names.length; i++) {
            callExt(b, "js_set", [callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, "$box$" + names[i])]),
                                  emitStr(b, "v"), callExt(b, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, names[i])])])
        }
    }
    // The tuple-return labels of the function whose body is currently being emitted.
    var retLabelStack = []
    function retLabelled(b, v) {
        if (retLabelStack.length == 0) { return v }
        var labels = retLabelStack[retLabelStack.length - 1]
        if (labels == null) { return v }
        return emitRelabel(b, v, labels)
    }
    function makeInit(items) {
        return {name: "init", params: items[0].params, body: items[1]}
    }
    // A top-level or nested function declaration. A second function of the same name
    // is an OVERLOAD: each candidate is declared under its own name$K and the plain
    // name resolves to a dispatcher that picks, at call time, the first candidate
    // whose declared parameter types accept the actual arguments. The candidate list
    // is shared, and every declaration statement re-declares the dispatcher, so by
    // the time any call runs the name refers to the complete set.
    var funcOverloads = {}
    // #if branch selection. items alternates {pcond} and {branch}; the answer is
    // the item list of the first branch whose condition is not statically false.
    // Nothing here evaluates os(...) / canImport(...) / swift(>=...): an ordinary
    // condition is treated as live, so the first branch wins.
    function poundLive(s) {
        var t = stripWs(s)
        if (t == "false") { return false }
        if (t == "0") { return false }
        return true
    }
    function poundPick(items) {
        var i = 0
        while (i + 1 < items.length) {
            if (poundLive(items[i].pcond)) { return items[i + 1].branch }
            i = i + 2
        }
        return []
    }
    function makeFunStmt(f) {
        regSig(f.name, f.params)
        var key = "$" + f.name
        var lst = hasOwn(funcOverloads, key) ? funcOverloads[key] : null
        if (lst == null) { lst = []; funcOverloads[key] = lst }
        lst.push({f: f})
        var slot = f.name + "$" + lst.length
        return function(b) {
            var idx = emitFunc(f.params, f.body, false, false, f.rlabels)
            var cloV = callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(idx), curScopeV])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, slot), cloV])
            if (lst.length == 1) {
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, f.name), cloV])
            } else {
                var didx = emitOverloadDispatch(f.name, lst)
                callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, f.name),
                                             callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(didx), curScopeV])])
            }
            return b
        }
    }
    // A nested function is the same declaration run as a statement of its body: the
    // closure is created over the current scope, so it captures the surrounding
    // locals and can call itself.
    function makeLocalFunStmt(f) { return makeFunStmt(f) }

    // The emitted overload dispatcher: for each candidate, in declaration order,
    // check the argument count against its required/maximum arity and the type of
    // every argument that has a declared parameter type, then tail-call it.
    function emitOverloadDispatch(name, lst) {
        funcCount++
        var idx = funcCount
        var f = m.NewFunc("jsf_" + idx, i64, [llvm.ir.NewParam("env", i64), llvm.ir.NewParam("args", i64)])
        var savedF = curF
        var savedScope = curScopeV
        var savedLoops = loopStack
        var savedTag = curFTag
        curF = f
        curFTag = idx
        loopStack = []
        var b = f.NewBlock("entry")
        var sc = callExt(b, "js_scope_new", [f.Params[0]])
        var argsV = f.Params[1]
        var nargs = callExt(b, "js_pylen", [argsV])
        for (var k = 0; k < lst.length; k++) {
            var P = lst[k].f.params
            var nextB = curF.NewBlock("")
            var req = 0
            var varia = false
            for (var q = 0; q < P.length; q++) {
                if (P[q].variadic) { varia = true }
                else if (!P[q].hasDefault) { req++ }
            }
            var okB = curF.NewBlock("")
            b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_ge", [nargs, emitNum(b, req)])), okB, nextB)
            b = okB
            if (!varia) {
                var okB2 = curF.NewBlock("")
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_le", [nargs, emitNum(b, P.length)])), okB2, nextB)
                b = okB2
            }
            for (var j = 0; j < P.length; j++) {
                if (P[j].variadic || P[j].type == "") { continue }
                var haveB = curF.NewBlock("")
                var contB = curF.NewBlock("")
                b.NewCondBr(truthy(b, callExt(b, "js_le", [nargs, emitNum(b, j)])), contB, haveB)
                var tv = callExt(haveB, "js_is_type", [callExt(haveB, "js_arg", [argsV, handle(j)]),
                                                       emitStr(haveB, P[j].type)])
                haveB.NewCondBr(truthy(haveB, tv), contB, nextB)
                b = contB
            }
            var fv = callExt(b, "js_kget", [sc, emitStr(b, name + "$" + (k + 1))])
            b.NewRet(callExt(b, "js_call", [fv, hUndef, argsV]))
            b = nextB
        }
        var fv0 = callExt(b, "js_kget", [sc, emitStr(b, name + "$1")])
        b.NewRet(callExt(b, "js_call", [fv0, hUndef, argsV]))
        curF = savedF
        curScopeV = savedScope
        loopStack = savedLoops
        curFTag = savedTag
        return idx
    }
    function makeProp(items) {
        if (items.length > 1) { return {prop: items[0], hasInit: true, init: items[1]} }
        return {prop: items[0], hasInit: false, init: null}
    }

    // items = [name, ({prop}|{method})...]
    function makeClassStmt(items) {
        var name = items[0]
        var props = []
        var stored = []
        var methods = []
        var hasInit = false
        for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) {
            var it = items[i]
            if (it.prop != undefined) {
                stored.push(it)
                if (it.hasInit) { props.push(it) }
            }
            if (it.method != undefined) {
                methods.push(it.method)
                if (it.method.name == "init") { hasInit = true; regSig(name, it.method.params) }
            }
        }
        // The memberwise initializer a struct without an explicit init gets for free:
        // one labelled parameter per stored property, in declaration order, defaulting
        // to the property's own initial value where it has one.
        var mparams = []
        if (!hasInit) {
            for (var s = 0; s < stored.length; s++) {
                mparams.push({name: stored[s].prop, label: stored[s].prop, type: "",
                              variadic: false, auto: false, inout: false,
                              hasDefault: stored[s].hasInit, dflt: stored[s].init})
            }
            regSig(name, mparams)
        }
        classNames[name] = 1
        return function(b) {
            var clsV = callExt(b, "js_obj_new", [])
            callExt(b, "js_set", [clsV, emitStr(b, "__isclass"), hTrue])
            callExt(b, "js_set", [clsV, emitStr(b, "__name"), emitStr(b, name)])
            callExt(b, "js_scope_decl", [curScopeV, emitStr(b, name), clsV])
            var ctorIdx = emitCtor(props)
            callExt(b, "js_set", [clsV, emitStr(b, "__ctor"), callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(ctorIdx), curScopeV])])
            for (var k = 0; k < methods.length; k++) {
                var idx = emitFunc(methods[k].params, methods[k].body, true, false, methods[k].rlabels)
                callExt(b, "js_set", [clsV, emitStr(b, methods[k].name), callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(idx), curScopeV])])
            }
            if (!hasInit) {
                var mwBody = function(bb) {
                    var thisV = callExt(bb, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(bb, "this")])
                    for (var q = 0; q < mparams.length; q++) {
                        callExt(bb, "js_set", [thisV, emitStr(bb, mparams[q].name),
                                               callExt(bb, "js_kget", [curScopeV, emitStr(bb, mparams[q].name)])])
                    }
                    return bb
                }
                var iidx = emitFunc(mparams, mwBody, true)
                callExt(b, "js_set", [clsV, emitStr(b, "init"), callExt(b, "js_closure", [handle(iidx), curScopeV])])
            }
            return b
        }
    }

    // items = [name, {ecase}...] -> a descriptor object of caseName -> caseName.
    function makeEnumStmt(items) {
        var name = items[0]
        var cases = []
        for (var i = 1; i < items.length; i++) { cases.push(items[i].ecase) }
        return function(b) {
            var eV = callExt(b, "js_obj_new", [])
            callExt(b, "js_set", [eV, emitStr(b, "__enum"), hTrue])
            for (var k = 0; k < cases.length; k++) {
                callExt(b, "js_set", [eV, emitStr(b, cases[k]), emitStr(b, cases[k])])
